(function(){
const sections=[
{id:'about',number:'01',title:'About Ads Journey',summary:'What Ads Journey is for and what the admin is responsible for.',keywords:'purpose admin responsibility system messenger shared record accurate meaningful update leads',intro:'Ads Journey is the working system for managing parent inquiries from first contact through enrollment.',content:"<h3>What Ads Journey is</h3><p>Ads Journey is the shared working system for managing every parent inquiry from the first contact until the journey ends in enrollment or a clear closed outcome.</p><p>Facebook Messenger may still be where the conversation with the parent happens. Ads Journey is where we record what that conversation means operationally: where the parent is in the journey, what has already happened, and what should happen next.</p><h3>Why we use it</h3><ul><li>To prevent inquiries and follow-ups from getting lost.</li><li>To give every admin the same view of what is happening with each parent.</li><li>To keep a clear history of meaningful actions and outcomes.</li><li>To make the next action obvious instead of relying on memory, Messenger threads, or separate sheets.</li><li>To give us reliable information about inquiries, trials, follow-ups, enrollments, and location performance.</li></ul><h3>Your responsibility as an admin</h3><p>Your job is not simply to move cards from one stage to another. Your job is to keep each Journey accurate.</p><ul><li>Make sure the Journey reflects what is actually happening with the parent.</li><li>Update the Journey after a meaningful change, such as an active conversation, a scheduled visit or trial, a result from the franchise, a planned follow-up, an enrollment, or a clear decision not to continue.</li><li>Add useful notes when they help the next admin understand what happened.</li><li>Use Search before creating a duplicate record when you think the parent may already exist.</li><li>Do not move or close a Journey simply to clear a column.</li></ul><h3>The most important rule</h3><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>The Journey should always reflect what is actually happening with the parent right now.</strong><br><br>If the conversation is active, the Journey should show that. If a trial is booked, it should show Scheduled. If we are waiting for the result, it should show Awaiting Outcome. If the parent is still deciding, it should show Follow-up / Decision. If they enroll, it should show Enrollment.</div><h3>What a good Journey record should tell you</h3><p>When any admin opens a Journey, they should be able to understand within a few seconds:</p><ul><li>Who the parent is and which location they are inquiring about.</li><li>What stage the parent is currently in.</li><li>What the last meaningful event was.</li><li>What needs to happen next.</li><li>Any important note that affects how the conversation should continue.</li></ul><h3>Think of the Journey as the shared memory</h3><p>The system should not depend on one admin remembering what happened, finding an old Messenger thread, or checking a separate sheet. If the Journey is kept current, another admin should be able to continue the work without guessing.</p>"},
{id:'journey-at-a-glance',number:'02',title:'The Journey at a Glance',summary:'How an inquiry moves from first contact to enrollment.',keywords:'stages flow inquiry enrollment overview active conversation scheduled outcome follow-up direct enrollment',intro:'This section will explain the complete journey in simple terms, showing how a parent moves through each stage and why the stages exist.',content:"<h3>The basic idea</h3><p>Every parent inquiry starts as a Journey. The Journey moves as the real situation with the parent changes.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>The stages are not a checklist.</strong><br><br>A parent does not need to pass through every stage. The Journey should move to the stage that best describes what is happening now.</div><h3>Stage 1 — Inquiry</h3><p>This is where a new inquiry begins. We are making the first contact, answering the first questions, and deciding what is actually happening with the lead.</p><p>From Stage 1, the Journey may move to Continue Conversation, Scheduled, Enrollment, or No Longer Interested depending on what happens.</p><h3>Stage 1A — Continue Conversation</h3><p>This is for a real, active conversation that is still moving but has not yet reached a scheduled visit, free trial, enrollment, or clear ending.</p><p>The conversation may be fast or slow. What matters is that the parent is still genuinely engaged and the conversation is still alive.</p><h3>Stage 2 — Scheduled</h3><p>The parent has committed to a visit or free trial. The appointment details are recorded and sent to the franchise.</p><p>The Journey stays here while we wait for the scheduled appointment.</p><h3>Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</h3><p>The scheduled visit or free trial has reached its time, and we now need to know what happened.</p><p>The admin gets the result from the franchise and records the outcome.</p><h3>Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision</h3><p>The parent has not enrolled yet, but there is still something to follow up on or a decision still being made.</p><p>This can include an interested parent who needs more time, a no-show, a cancelled appointment, or another situation where the conversation should continue.</p><h3>Stage 5 — Enrollment</h3><p>The parent has enrolled. This is the successful completion of the Journey.</p><h3>Not every Journey follows the same path</h3><p>Some common paths are:</p><ul><li><strong>Inquiry → Continue Conversation → Scheduled → Awaiting Outcome → Follow-up / Decision → Enrollment</strong></li><li><strong>Inquiry → Scheduled → Awaiting Outcome → Enrollment</strong></li><li><strong>Inquiry → Continue Conversation → Enrollment</strong> when the parent enrolls directly without a visit or free trial.</li><li><strong>Inquiry → No Longer Interested</strong> when the parent clearly declines or the Journey has genuinely ended.</li><li><strong>Follow-up / Decision → Scheduled</strong> when another visit or free trial is arranged.</li></ul><h3>What moves a Journey forward</h3><p>A Journey moves because something meaningful happened in the real conversation or appointment — not because a certain amount of time passed and not because we want to clear the board.</p><ul><li>The parent begins a real conversation → Continue Conversation.</li><li>A visit or free trial is booked → Scheduled.</li><li>The appointment reaches its scheduled time → Awaiting Outcome.</li><li>The result requires more parent contact → Follow-up / Decision.</li><li>The parent enrolls → Enrollment.</li><li>The parent clearly ends the conversation → No Longer Interested.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>When you are unsure which stage to use, ask one question:</strong><br><br>“What is actually happening with this parent right now?”<br><br>The answer should normally tell you which stage the Journey belongs in.</div>"},
{id:'main-dashboard',number:'03',title:'Main Dashboard',summary:'Counters, working queue, Journey cards, and how the board is organized.',keywords:'dashboard counters active scheduled franchise update due follow up enrolled board cards sorting working queue due now',intro:'This section explains what you see on the main screen, what the counters mean, how the stage columns work, and how Journeys are ordered inside each stage.',content:"<h3>What the dashboard is for</h3><p>The Main Dashboard is your working view of the parent Journeys that currently need to be managed. It lets you see the overall workload, where each parent is in the Journey, and which records need attention first.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>The dashboard is a working queue, not a permanent list of every record.</strong><br><br>Older, closed, dormant, or completed records may no longer appear on the board. Use Search when you need to find a Journey that is not currently visible.</div><h3>The counters at the top</h3><p>The five counters give you a quick summary of the locations currently selected in the Franchise Filter.</p><ul><li><strong>Active</strong> — the total number of Journeys currently visible on the working board.</li><li><strong>Scheduled</strong> — Journeys in Stage 2 with a visit or free trial scheduled.</li><li><strong>Franchise Update Due</strong> — Journeys in Stage 3 where the scheduled time has arrived and we need the result from the franchise.</li><li><strong>Follow Up</strong> — Stage 4 Journeys where a parent follow-up is due now. This is not the total number of records in Stage 4.</li><li><strong>Enrolled</strong> — enrolled Journeys that are still being shown on the current working board.</li></ul><p>When you change the Franchise Filter, the board and these counters update to match the selected locations.</p><h3>The Working Queue</h3><p>The board is divided into six columns. Each column represents the parent’s current stage:</p><ul><li><strong>Stage 1 — Inquiry</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 1A — Continue Conversation</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong></li></ul><p>The number in the top-right of each column is the number of Journeys currently visible in that stage.</p><h3>Reading a Journey card</h3><p>Every card represents one parent Journey. The card gives you enough information to decide what to look at next without opening every record.</p><p>Depending on the stage, a card may show:</p><ul><li>The parent’s Facebook name.</li><li>The franchise location.</li><li>The current status.</li><li>The next action, such as Continue Conversation, Send Details to Franchise, Get Result From Franchise, or Follow Up With Parent.</li><li>The date or time connected to the next action.</li></ul><p>Stage 1 cards show when the inquiry first came in. Cards in later stages focus more on the current status and next required action.</p><h3>Due now</h3><p>If a Journey has a required action whose time has arrived or passed, the card may be marked <strong>Due now</strong> and visually emphasized.</p><p>That does not mean you should automatically change the stage. Open the Journey, understand what is due, and complete the correct real-world action.</p><h3>How records are ordered</h3><p>The board automatically sorts each stage so the most useful records appear first:</p><ul><li><strong>Inquiry</strong> — newest inquiries first.</li><li><strong>Continue Conversation</strong> — most recently active conversations first.</li><li><strong>Scheduled</strong> — earliest upcoming appointment or action first.</li><li><strong>Awaiting Outcome</strong> — earliest due result first.</li><li><strong>Follow-up / Decision</strong> — earliest due follow-up first.</li><li><strong>Enrollment</strong> — most recently updated enrollments first.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>You do not need to manually organize the board.</strong><br><br>Keep each Journey accurate and keep its next action current. The dashboard will use that information to place and order the record correctly.</div><h3>Opening a Journey</h3><p>Click a Journey card to open it. The Journey window contains the detailed information, timeline, notes, current status, and the actions available for that stage.</p><p>The dashboard gives you the overview. The Journey itself is where you understand the record and make the next update.</p><h3>Other controls on the dashboard</h3><p>The top of the dashboard also includes New Inquiry, Search, Franchise Filter, Help, and Maintenance. These tools have their own sections in this manual. For normal day-to-day work, the Working Queue should remain your main view.</p>"},
{id:'stage-1',number:'04',title:'Stage 1 — Inquiry',summary:'New inquiries and the first decisions an admin makes.',keywords:'stage 1 inquiry free trial visit continue conversation enroll no longer interested parent child session schedule message',intro:'This section explains what belongs in Stage 1 and how to choose the correct next step for a new parent inquiry.',content:"<h3>What Stage 1 means</h3><p>Stage 1 is where a new parent inquiry begins. The parent has contacted us, the Journey has been created, and the first meaningful decision has not yet been recorded.</p><p>Your job in Stage 1 is to understand what is happening in the conversation and choose the next step that matches the parent’s real situation.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not move a Journey just to clear Stage 1.</strong><br><br>Choose the option that describes what actually happened with the parent.</div><h3>Opening a Stage 1 Journey</h3><p>Click the parent’s card in the Inquiry column. The Journey window opens with the parent, location, current stage, current status, next step, and Journey Timeline.</p><p>Under <strong>Choose the next step</strong>, you have four main choices: Free Trial, Visit, Continue Conversation, and Enroll. A separate <strong>No Longer Interested</strong> action is also available.</p><h3>Free Trial</h3><p>Choose <strong>Free Trial</strong> when the parent has agreed to a specific free trial appointment.</p><p>Enter the appointment information:</p><ul><li><strong>Parent name</strong> — the parent’s real name.</li><li><strong>Session interested in</strong> — choose the appropriate session when known.</li><li><strong>Date and time</strong> — the agreed trial schedule.</li><li><strong>Child name</strong> — required for the appointment record.</li><li><strong>Age</strong> — years and months when known.</li><li><strong>Notes</strong> — anything useful the franchise should know.</li></ul><p>Select <strong>Save Schedule</strong>. The Journey moves to <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>, where the franchise handoff is completed.</p><h3>Visit</h3><p>Choose <strong>Visit</strong> when the parent has agreed to come to the playschool for a visit rather than a free trial.</p><p>Complete the same appointment information and select <strong>Save Schedule</strong>. The Journey moves to <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>A visit or free trial should only be scheduled after the parent has actually agreed to the appointment.</strong><br><br>Do not create a schedule just because you suggested a date or asked whether they would like to visit.</div><h3>Continue Conversation</h3><p>Choose <strong>Continue Conversation</strong> when the parent is genuinely engaged but the conversation has not yet reached a visit, free trial, enrollment, or clear ending.</p><p>You may add a short Message Note describing what was sent or what the conversation is about. The note is optional, but it can help another admin understand the context.</p><p>Select <strong>Save to Stage 1A</strong>. The Journey moves to <strong>Stage 1A — Continue Conversation</strong> and the message is recorded in the Journey Timeline.</p><p>Examples include a parent asking more questions about rates, schedules, age groups, requirements, or available options before deciding what to do next.</p><h3>Enroll</h3><p>Choose <strong>Enroll</strong> when the parent enrolls directly from the inquiry or active conversation without needing a visit or free trial first.</p><p>You may add an Enrollment Note, then select <strong>Confirm Enrolled</strong>. The Journey moves directly to <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</p><p>Only use Enroll when the enrollment has actually happened. Interest, intent, or saying “I want to enroll” is not the same as a completed enrollment unless the required enrollment step has been completed.</p><h3>No Longer Interested</h3><p>Choose <strong>No Longer Interested</strong> when the parent has clearly decided not to continue and the Journey is genuinely finished.</p><p>A note is required. Record the reason or useful context, then select <strong>Confirm No Longer Interested</strong>. The Journey closes and leaves the working board.</p><p>Do not use No Longer Interested simply because the parent has not replied quickly. A slow reply is not the same as a clear decision to stop.</p><h3>How to decide what to choose</h3><ul><li>Parent agreed to a free trial → <strong>Free Trial</strong>.</li><li>Parent agreed to a visit → <strong>Visit</strong>.</li><li>Conversation is active but no appointment or enrollment yet → <strong>Continue Conversation</strong>.</li><li>Parent has actually enrolled → <strong>Enroll</strong>.</li><li>Parent clearly ended the inquiry → <strong>No Longer Interested</strong>.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>The important question is always: “What actually happened with this parent?”</strong><br><br>The answer determines the correct Stage 1 action.</div><h3>After you save</h3><p>The dashboard updates automatically. The Journey will appear in its new stage, and the action you recorded becomes part of the Journey Timeline so another admin can understand what happened.</p>"},
{id:'stage-1a',number:'05',title:'Stage 1A — Continue Conversation',summary:'Active parent conversations that have not reached a scheduled outcome yet.',keywords:'stage 1a continue conversation active conversation message reply free trial visit enroll no longer interested',intro:'This section explains when a Journey belongs in Stage 1A, how to keep an active conversation current, and what moves it to the next stage.',content:"<h3>What Stage 1A means</h3><p>Stage 1A is for a parent who is genuinely engaged in an active conversation, but has not yet reached a scheduled visit, free trial, enrollment, or clear ending.</p><p>The parent may still be asking questions, comparing options, checking schedules, discussing rates, or deciding what will work for their child.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Stage 1A means the conversation is still alive.</strong><br><br>The parent does not need to reply immediately. What matters is that there is still a real conversation to continue.</div><h3>How a Journey reaches Stage 1A</h3><p>A Journey normally moves here from Stage 1 when the admin chooses <strong>Continue Conversation</strong> and records the parent message or ongoing discussion.</p><p>Once in Stage 1A, the card appears in the Continue Conversation column and the next step remains <strong>Continue Conversation</strong>.</p><h3>Opening a Stage 1A Journey</h3><p>Click the parent’s card in the Continue Conversation column. The Journey window shows the current stage, current status, next step, and the Journey Timeline.</p><p>The same action choices remain available because an active conversation can still lead directly to a Free Trial, Visit, Enrollment, or a clear closed outcome.</p><h3>Continue Conversation again</h3><p>If you send another meaningful message and the conversation is still active, choose <strong>Continue Conversation</strong> again.</p><p>You can add a Message Note describing what was sent or what changed. When you select <strong>Save to Stage 1A</strong>, the Journey stays in Stage 1A and the new message is added to the Journey Timeline.</p><p>This is useful because it shows that the conversation is still being worked and gives the next admin context about the latest meaningful contact.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>You do not need to create a new Journey every time the parent sends another message.</strong><br><br>Keep using the same Journey and continue adding meaningful updates to its timeline.</div><h3>When the parent books a Free Trial</h3><p>If the active conversation results in a confirmed free trial, choose <strong>Free Trial</strong> and enter the parent name, session, date, time, child name, age, and any useful notes.</p><p>Select <strong>Save Schedule</strong>. The Journey moves from Stage 1A to <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</p><h3>When the parent books a Visit</h3><p>If the parent confirms a playschool visit instead, choose <strong>Visit</strong>, complete the appointment details, and select <strong>Save Schedule</strong>.</p><p>The Journey moves to <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</p><h3>When the parent enrolls directly</h3><p>If the parent actually completes enrollment during the active conversation without first scheduling a visit or free trial, choose <strong>Enroll</strong>.</p><p>Add an Enrollment Note when useful and select <strong>Confirm Enrolled</strong>. The Journey moves directly to <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</p><h3>When the parent is no longer interested</h3><p>If the parent clearly says they will not continue, choose <strong>No Longer Interested</strong>.</p><p>A note is required so there is a clear record of why the Journey ended. After confirmation, the Journey closes and leaves the working board.</p><p>Do not use this simply because the parent has gone quiet for a short period. A quiet conversation and a clear decision not to continue are different things.</p><h3>What should stay in Stage 1A</h3><p>Keep the Journey in Stage 1A while the conversation is still active and none of these has happened yet:</p><ul><li>No visit or free trial has been confirmed.</li><li>No enrollment has been completed.</li><li>The parent has not clearly ended the inquiry.</li></ul><p>Examples include a parent asking follow-up questions, discussing which session may fit, checking with a spouse, asking about rates or requirements, or taking some time to decide while still engaged.</p><h3>What moves the Journey out of Stage 1A</h3><ul><li>Confirmed free trial → <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</li><li>Confirmed visit → <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</li><li>Completed enrollment → <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</li><li>Clear decision not to continue → <strong>Journey closed as No Longer Interested</strong>.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not move the Journey because the conversation feels slow.</strong><br><br>Move it only when the real situation changes.</div>"},
{id:'stage-2',number:'06',title:'Stage 2 — Scheduled',summary:'Visits, free trials, franchise handoff, rescheduling, and cancellations.',keywords:'stage 2 scheduled visit free trial franchise handoff copy message mark sent waiting appointment reschedule cancel awaiting outcome',intro:'This section explains what happens after a visit or free trial is scheduled, including the franchise handoff, waiting for the appointment, rescheduling, and cancellation.',content:"<h3>What Stage 2 means</h3><p>Stage 2 means the parent has committed to a specific <strong>visit or free trial</strong>. The appointment has been recorded and the next responsibility is to make sure the franchise receives the correct details.</p><p>The Journey remains in Scheduled while we are waiting for the appointment to happen.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Scheduled means there is a real confirmed appointment.</strong><br><br>Do not use Stage 2 for a suggested date, a possible visit, or a parent who has not yet agreed.</div><h3>When a Journey first enters Stage 2</h3><p>After a visit or free trial is saved from Stage 1 or Stage 1A, the Journey opens the <strong>Franchise Handoff</strong> section.</p><p>You will see the scheduled date and time, the location, and the appointment details that were entered for the parent and child.</p><p>At this point the status is <strong>Ready to Send</strong> and the next step is <strong>Send Details to Franchise</strong>.</p><h3>Review the appointment details</h3><p>Before sending anything, check that the appointment information is correct. The prepared franchise message can include:</p><ul><li>Visit or Free Trial.</li><li>Parent name and Facebook name.</li><li>Child name and age.</li><li>Session.</li><li>Date and time.</li><li>Any useful notes for the franchise.</li></ul><p>Use the appointment details control when you need to review the complete information before sending it.</p><h3>Copy Message</h3><p>Select <strong>Copy Message</strong> to copy the prepared appointment information. Send that information to the correct franchise through the normal franchise communication channel.</p><p>Copying the message does <strong>not</strong> mean the franchise has been notified. It only copies the prepared text.</p><h3>Mark as Sent</h3><p>After you have actually sent the appointment details to the franchise, select <strong>Mark as Sent</strong>.</p><p>The Journey status changes to <strong>Details Sent to Franchise</strong>, and the next step becomes <strong>Wait for Visit / Free Trial</strong>.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not click Mark as Sent before sending the details.</strong><br><br>This button is the system record that the franchise has actually been notified.</div><h3>Expected franchise update</h3><p>Once the details are marked as sent, the Journey shows the expected franchise update time. The Journey stays in Stage 2 while we wait for the scheduled appointment.</p><p>You do not need to manually move the Journey when the appointment time arrives. When the expected time is reached, the dashboard automatically moves the Journey into <strong>Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</strong> so the result can be collected from the franchise.</p><h3>Reschedule</h3><p>Use <strong>Reschedule</strong> when the appointment is still happening but the session, date, or time has changed.</p><p>Enter the new:</p><ul><li>Session.</li><li>Date.</li><li>Time.</li><li>Note, when useful, explaining the change.</li></ul><p>Select <strong>Save New Schedule</strong>. The Journey stays in the scheduled workflow with the updated appointment information, and the change is recorded in the Journey Timeline.</p><p>If the franchise had already received the old appointment details, make sure the updated appointment information is also communicated to them.</p><h3>Cancel Appointment</h3><p>Use <strong>Cancel Appointment</strong> when the scheduled visit or free trial will no longer happen.</p><p>A cancellation note is required. Record why the appointment was cancelled, then select <strong>Confirm Cancel</strong>.</p><p>The cancelled appointment is recorded in the Journey history and it is no longer treated as an active scheduled appointment. The Journey can then continue through the appropriate follow-up or decision path based on the parent’s real situation.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Cancellation does not automatically mean the parent is no longer interested.</strong><br><br>A parent may cancel because of schedule, illness, travel, or another temporary reason. Record what actually happened and continue the Journey accordingly.</div><h3>What you should check in Stage 2</h3><ul><li>Is the appointment information correct?</li><li>Were the details actually sent to the franchise?</li><li>Was Mark as Sent used only after they were sent?</li><li>Has the appointment changed and does it need to be rescheduled?</li><li>Has the appointment been cancelled?</li></ul><h3>What moves the Journey out of Stage 2</h3><p>The normal path is:</p><p><strong>Scheduled → Details Sent to Franchise → Wait for Visit / Free Trial → Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</strong></p><p>The system handles the move into Stage 3 when the expected appointment/update time arrives. The admin’s responsibility is to keep the appointment and franchise handoff accurate before that happens.</p>"},
{id:'stage-3',number:'07',title:'Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome',summary:'Getting the result after a scheduled visit or free trial.',keywords:'stage 3 awaiting outcome franchise result trial visit',intro:'This section will explain when a journey moves into Awaiting Outcome and how to record what the franchise reports after the appointment.'},
{id:'stage-4',number:'08',title:'Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision',summary:'Parent follow-up after a visit, trial, no-show, cancellation, or another decision point.',keywords:'stage 4 follow-up decision interested no show cancelled follow up later enrolled reschedule no longer interested due now',intro:'This section explains why a Journey enters Stage 4, how to manage follow-up, and what moves the Journey forward or closes it.',content:"<h3>What Stage 4 means</h3><p>Stage 4 is where we continue the Journey when the parent has not enrolled yet but there is still a real decision or follow-up to manage.</p><p>A Journey may arrive here after a franchise result such as <strong>Interested</strong>, <strong>No Show</strong>, or <strong>Cancelled</strong>. It can also remain here when an admin deliberately schedules another parent follow-up.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Stage 4 is not a waiting room for forgotten leads.</strong><br><br>If the Journey stays here, there should be a clear reason and, when appropriate, a real next follow-up date.</div><h3>Opening a Stage 4 Journey</h3><p>Click the parent’s card in the Follow-up / Decision column. The Journey window shows the previous appointment information, current status, next action, and Journey Timeline.</p><p>Depending on what happened previously, the status may show something such as <strong>Follow-up Due</strong>, <strong>No Show</strong>, or <strong>Appointment Cancelled</strong>.</p><p>The Stage 4 actions are:</p><ul><li><strong>Enrolled</strong></li><li><strong>Reschedule</strong></li><li><strong>Follow Up Later</strong></li><li><strong>No Longer Interested</strong></li></ul><h3>Follow Up Later</h3><p>Choose <strong>Follow Up Later</strong> when the parent is still a real potential enrollment but the next conversation should happen at a later date.</p><p>Enter the follow-up date, time, and a note explaining what you need to remember or what the parent asked you to do.</p><p>Select <strong>Save Follow-up</strong>. The Journey stays in <strong>Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision</strong> with the new follow-up time recorded.</p><p>When the follow-up time arrives, the card becomes due and may be shown as <strong>Due now</strong>. It also contributes to the <strong>Follow Up</strong> counter on the dashboard.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not use Follow Up Later without a real reason.</strong><br><br>The date should represent when we genuinely intend to contact the parent again, not just a way to move the card out of the way.</div><h3>Reschedule</h3><p>Choose <strong>Reschedule</strong> when another visit or free trial has been agreed to.</p><p>Enter the session, new date, new time, and any useful note. Select <strong>Reschedule</strong>.</p><p>The Journey moves back to <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong> with the new appointment details.</p><p>Because this is a new confirmed appointment, the franchise handoff process begins again and the updated details must be sent to the franchise.</p><h3>Enrolled</h3><p>Choose <strong>Enrolled</strong> when the parent has actually completed enrollment during the follow-up process.</p><p>You may add an Enrollment Note, then select <strong>Confirm Enrolled</strong>. The Journey moves to <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</p><p>If a previous enrollment was undone and the parent later enrolls again, the action may appear as <strong>Re-Enroll</strong>. Use it only when the new enrollment is genuinely confirmed.</p><h3>No Longer Interested</h3><p>Choose <strong>No Longer Interested</strong> when the parent clearly decides not to continue and there is no meaningful reason to keep following up.</p><p>A note is required. Record why the Journey is ending, then select <strong>Confirm No Longer Interested</strong>.</p><p>The Journey closes and leaves the active working board, while its history remains available through Search.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>No reply is not automatically No Longer Interested.</strong><br><br>Use the actual conversation and context. If another follow-up is appropriate, schedule it. Close the Journey only when the situation genuinely supports closing it.</div><h3>Common Stage 4 situations</h3><ul><li><strong>Interested after trial</strong> — parent liked the experience but needs time to decide → Follow Up Later.</li><li><strong>No Show</strong> — contact the parent; if they want another appointment → Reschedule.</li><li><strong>Cancelled</strong> — find out whether they want another date; if yes → Reschedule.</li><li><strong>Needs more time</strong> — schedule the next reasonable contact → Follow Up Later.</li><li><strong>Completed enrollment</strong> → Enrolled.</li><li><strong>Clearly declined</strong> → No Longer Interested.</li></ul><h3>How to decide what happens next</h3><ul><li>Another conversation is needed later → <strong>Follow Up Later → stays in Stage 4</strong>.</li><li>Another visit or free trial is confirmed → <strong>Reschedule → Stage 2</strong>.</li><li>Parent completes enrollment → <strong>Enrolled → Stage 5</strong>.</li><li>Journey has clearly ended → <strong>No Longer Interested → closed</strong>.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>The purpose of Stage 4 is to keep a real opportunity moving without losing it.</strong><br><br>Every Journey here should have a clear next action or a clear ending.</div>"},
{id:'stage-5',number:'09',title:'Stage 5 — Enrollment',summary:'The successful end of the Journey and how to correct an enrollment when necessary.',keywords:'stage 5 enrollment enrolled enrollment reported undo enrollment re-enroll correction timeline',intro:'This section explains what Stage 5 means, what information is shown after enrollment, and how to correct an enrollment without losing the Journey history.',content:"<h3>What Stage 5 means</h3><p>Stage 5 means the parent has actually enrolled. This is the successful completion of the advertising Journey.</p><p>A Journey can reach Stage 5 directly from Stage 1 or Stage 1A, from the franchise result in Stage 3, or from Stage 4 during follow-up.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Only record Enrollment when the enrollment has actually happened.</strong><br><br>Interest, a promise to enroll, or asking how to enroll is not yet an enrollment. Stage 5 should represent a real completed enrollment.</div><h3>Opening an enrolled Journey</h3><p>Click the card in the Enrollment column to open the Journey.</p><p>The Enrollment section shows:</p><ul><li>The parent and franchise location.</li><li>The child name when it was captured earlier in the Journey.</li><li>The date and time the enrollment was reported.</li><li>The enrollment note that was recorded.</li><li>The complete Journey Timeline showing how the parent reached enrollment.</li></ul><p>The Journey stage is shown as <strong>Enrolled</strong>. Depending on the current processing state, the status may also indicate that the enrollment has been reported.</p><h3>Why the Journey history still matters</h3><p>Enrollment is the end result, but the history leading to it remains important. The timeline can show the original inquiry, conversations, appointments, franchise handoffs, trial or visit results, follow-ups, and finally the enrollment.</p><p>This gives us a reliable record of what actually led to the successful outcome and allows the Journey to remain useful later for performance and analysis.</p><h3>Undo Enrollment</h3><p>Use <strong>Undo Enrollment</strong> only when the enrollment was recorded incorrectly or the situation genuinely needs to be corrected.</p><p>Select <strong>Undo Enrollment</strong>, enter the reason for the correction, and then select <strong>Confirm Undo</strong>.</p><p>The reason is required. The system records the enrollment reversal in the Journey Timeline instead of deleting the original enrollment history.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Undo Enrollment is a correction tool, not a normal Journey action.</strong><br><br>Do not undo an enrollment just because something changed later. Use it when the enrollment record itself should no longer be treated as the current outcome.</div><h3>What happens after Undo Enrollment</h3><p>The Journey returns to the active follow-up flow so the parent’s current situation can be handled correctly.</p><p>The previous enrollment remains visible in the Journey history together with the reason it was undone. If the parent later enrolls again, Stage 4 may show the action as <strong>Re-Enroll</strong>.</p><h3>Re-Enroll</h3><p><strong>Re-Enroll</strong> is used when an earlier enrollment was undone and the parent later genuinely enrolls again.</p><p>Confirm the new enrollment just as you would any other enrollment. The new enrollment is added to the Journey history, preserving the complete sequence instead of replacing the earlier events.</p><h3>What admins should check before recording Enrollment</h3><ul><li>Has the parent actually completed the required enrollment step?</li><li>Is this the correct parent and franchise location?</li><li>Is there a useful enrollment note that should be recorded?</li><li>Are you recording a real enrollment rather than interest or intent?</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Stage 5 should be trustworthy.</strong><br><br>Every Journey recorded as enrolled becomes part of our enrollment and conversion information. Accuracy here directly affects how we understand franchise and advertising performance.</div>"},
{id:'reading-a-journey',number:'10',title:'Opening and Reading a Journey',summary:'How to understand a Journey quickly before taking action.',keywords:'open journey parent location child stage status next step action timeline history notes appointment details',intro:'This section explains how to read the Journey window so you can quickly understand who the parent is, what is happening now, what happened before, and what should happen next.',content:"<h3>Opening a Journey</h3><p>Click any Journey card on the dashboard to open the full Parent Journey.</p><p>The Journey panel brings together the current situation and the important history in one place. Before taking any action, read the Journey first.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not start by clicking an action button.</strong><br><br>First understand the parent, the current stage, the current status, the next step, and the recent timeline.</div><h3>1. Parent information</h3><p>At the top of the Journey you will see the parent and location information.</p><ul><li><strong>Parent name</strong> — normally the Facebook name or the real parent name when it has been captured.</li><li><strong>Franchise location</strong> — the location this inquiry belongs to.</li><li><strong>Facebook name</strong> — shown with the location so you can match the Journey to the Messenger conversation.</li><li><strong>Child name</strong> — shown when it was captured during scheduling or another part of the Journey.</li></ul><p>This information helps make sure you are working on the correct parent before making any changes.</p><h3>2. Journey Stage</h3><p><strong>Journey Stage</strong> tells you where the parent currently is in the overall process.</p><p>Examples include New Inquiry, Continue Conversation, Appointment Scheduled, Awaiting Franchise Update, Parent Follow-up, and Enrolled.</p><p>The stage answers the question: <strong>“Where is this parent in the Journey?”</strong></p><h3>3. Current Status</h3><p><strong>Current Status</strong> gives more detail about what is happening inside that stage.</p><p>Examples include New Inquiry, Active Conversation, Ready to Send to Franchise, Details Sent to Franchise, Waiting for Franchise Result, Follow-up Due, No Show, Appointment Cancelled, and Enrolled.</p><p>The status answers: <strong>“What is the current condition of this Journey?”</strong></p><h3>4. Next Step</h3><p><strong>Next Step</strong> tells you what the system expects to happen next.</p><p>Examples include Continue Conversation, Send Details to Franchise, Wait for Visit / Free Trial, Get Result From Franchise, Follow Up With Parent, or No Action Needed.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Stage, Status, and Next Step work together.</strong><br><br>Stage tells you where the parent is. Status tells you what is happening there. Next Step tells you what should happen next.</div><h3>5. The action area</h3><p>The middle of the Journey changes depending on the current stage. It shows only the actions that make sense for that part of the Journey.</p><p>For example:</p><ul><li>Stage 1 and Stage 1A show Free Trial, Visit, Continue Conversation, Enroll, and No Longer Interested.</li><li>Stage 2 shows the franchise handoff, appointment details, Mark as Sent, Reschedule, and Cancel Appointment.</li><li>Stage 3 shows the franchise result choices and Reschedule.</li><li>Stage 4 shows Enrolled, Reschedule, Follow Up Later, and No Longer Interested.</li><li>Stage 5 shows the enrollment record and Undo Enrollment.</li></ul><p>Use the action that matches what actually happened. Do not choose an action simply because it is available.</p><h3>6. Appointment and detail sections</h3><p>If the Journey has a visit or free trial, the panel may show the scheduled date and time, location, appointment type, parent and child information, session, and notes.</p><p>Use the expandable appointment details when you need to review the original information or understand a later reschedule, cancellation, no-show, or follow-up.</p><h3>7. Journey Timeline</h3><p>The <strong>Journey Timeline</strong> is the history of meaningful events in the Journey. The newest events appear first.</p><p>The timeline can include events such as:</p><ul><li>Inquiry created.</li><li>Message sent to parent.</li><li>Visit or free trial scheduled.</li><li>Details sent to franchise.</li><li>Appointment rescheduled or cancelled.</li><li>No show.</li><li>Visit or trial completed.</li><li>Parent interested or not interested.</li><li>Follow-up scheduled or completed.</li><li>Enrollment reported, undone, or processed.</li><li>Journey closed, dormant, or reactivated.</li></ul><p>Each timeline entry may also include a note, appointment information, or date and time.</p><h3>How to read a Journey quickly</h3><p>When you open a record, use this order:</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> Confirm the parent and franchise.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> Read Journey Stage.</li><li><strong>3.</strong> Read Current Status.</li><li><strong>4.</strong> Read Next Step.</li><li><strong>5.</strong> Look at the most recent Timeline entries.</li><li><strong>6.</strong> Review appointment details or notes if needed.</li><li><strong>7.</strong> Take the correct action.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>A good Journey should make sense without asking another admin what happened.</strong><br><br>If the stage, status, next step, and timeline are kept accurate, any admin should be able to open the Journey and continue the work confidently.</div>"},
{id:'search',number:'11',title:'Search',summary:'Finding active, closed, enrolled, dormant, and older Journeys.',keywords:'search facebook profile url username name inquiry id journey id parent child active closed dormant enrolled view record open reactivate duplicate old record',intro:'This section explains how to find Journeys that are not currently visible on the working board, review their history, and reactivate a closed Journey when the parent returns.',content:"<h3>What Search is for</h3><p>The dashboard is a working queue, so not every Journey will always be visible there. <strong>Search</strong> lets you find records beyond the current board, including active, dormant, enrolled, closed, and older Journeys.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Use Search before creating a new Journey when you think the parent may already exist.</strong><br><br>This helps prevent duplicate records and keeps the parent’s full history in one Journey.</div><h3>Opening Search</h3><p>Select <strong>Search</strong> at the top of the dashboard. The Journey Search window opens with a search box.</p><p>You can search using information such as:</p><ul><li>Facebook profile URL.</li><li>Facebook username.</li><li>Parent or Facebook name.</li><li>Child name.</li><li>Inquiry ID.</li><li>Journey ID.</li></ul><p>Enter what you know and select <strong>Search</strong>, or press Enter.</p><h3>Reading the search results</h3><p>Each result shows the parent, franchise location, Journey stage, current status, and record state.</p><p>The record state tells you whether the Journey is currently:</p><ul><li><strong>Active</strong> — the Journey is still active work.</li><li><strong>Closed</strong> — the Journey was previously ended.</li><li><strong>Dormant</strong> — the record is kept in history but is not currently part of active board work.</li></ul><p>Enrolled and older records can also appear in Search even when they are no longer visible on the working board.</p><h3>View Record</h3><p>Select <strong>View Record</strong> when you want to inspect a Journey without changing it.</p><p>The result expands to show the current stage, current status, Facebook name, and Journey history. The history includes meaningful events and notes in reverse chronological order.</p><p>Select <strong>Hide Record</strong> to collapse it again.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>View Record is the safest first step when you are not sure whether you found the correct parent.</strong><br><br>Review the history before opening, reactivating, or creating anything new.</div><h3>Open an active Journey</h3><p>If the result is Active, an <strong>Open</strong> button is available.</p><p>If that Journey is currently visible on the selected franchise board, Open closes Search and opens the normal Parent Journey panel so you can continue working on it.</p><p>If the Journey is active but not currently visible on the selected franchise board, Search will tell you that instead of opening the wrong board record.</p><h3>Reactivate a closed Journey</h3><p>If a parent with a closed Journey contacts us again and the old Journey should continue, select <strong>Reactivate Journey</strong>.</p><p>The system records the reactivation, reloads the working board, and updates the search result. The old history is preserved so the returning conversation stays connected to what happened before.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Reactivate the existing Journey when the same parent’s old conversation is continuing.</strong><br><br>Do not create a new Journey simply because the old one is closed.</div><h3>Dormant Journeys</h3><p>Dormant Journeys can be found and reviewed through Search. They are identified as <strong>Dormant journey</strong> and are not opened as normal active board work from the Search result.</p><p>Use View Record to understand the history before deciding what should happen next.</p><h3>Search and the Franchise Filter</h3><p>Search is broader than the visible working board. Finding a record does not necessarily mean that its franchise is currently selected on the dashboard.</p><p>This is why an active Search result can exist even when its card is not visible in the current board view.</p><h3>When a duplicate is detected during New Inquiry</h3><p>If New Inquiry detects that the Facebook profile already has an inquiry record, the system can offer <strong>Open Existing Journey</strong>.</p><p>When possible, the app finds the existing Journey, includes its franchise in the current selection, reloads the board, and opens the existing record. If it cannot open it directly, it brings you to Search with that record available.</p><h3>A simple Search routine</h3><ul><li>Search for the parent before creating a duplicate.</li><li>Use View Record to confirm the identity and history.</li><li>If Active, use Open when the Journey is on the current board.</li><li>If Closed and the same Journey is continuing, use Reactivate Journey.</li><li>If Dormant, review the record before deciding what should happen next.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>The goal of Search is continuity.</strong><br><br>We want one accurate history for the parent whenever possible, not separate records that make the real Journey harder to understand.</div>"},
{id:'franchise-filter',number:'12',title:'Franchise Filter',summary:'Choosing which locations you are currently viewing.',keywords:'franchise filter locations branches select all',intro:'This section will explain how the franchise filter changes the records shown on the dashboard and how to work with one or many locations.'},
{id:'maintenance',number:'13',title:'Maintenance',summary:'Batch Import, Admin Activity, Location Performance, and Marketing Performance.',keywords:'maintenance batch import json backfill duplicate admin activity location performance marketing performance reporting snapshot',intro:'This section explains the tools kept under Maintenance, what each one is for, and when admins should use them.',content:"<h3>What Maintenance is for</h3><p>The <strong>Maintenance</strong> menu contains tools that support the Ads Journey system but are not part of the normal parent-by-parent workflow.</p><p>Use these tools for backfilling inquiry records, reviewing admin activity, and checking reporting areas.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not use Maintenance tools to replace the normal Journey workflow.</strong><br><br>New inquiries, conversations, scheduling, outcomes, follow-ups, and enrollments should still be handled through the main Journey system.</div><h3>Batch Import</h3><p><strong>Batch Import</strong> is a backfill tool for creating multiple inquiry records for one franchise at the same time.</p><p>Use it when historical or externally prepared inquiries need to be added into Ads Journey in bulk rather than entered one at a time through New Inquiry.</p><h3>How Batch Import works</h3><p>Open <strong>Maintenance → Batch Import</strong>, then:</p><ul><li>Select the <strong>Branch / location</strong> for the entire batch.</li><li>Paste the inquiry records as a <strong>JSON array</strong>.</li><li>Select <strong>Import Batch</strong>.</li></ul><p>Each record must contain:</p><ul><li><strong>facebook_name</strong></li><li><strong>facebook_profile_url</strong></li><li><strong>first_message_at</strong></li></ul><p>Optional fields include <strong>facebook_username</strong>, <strong>ad_id</strong>, <strong>inquiry_type</strong>, and <strong>initial_note</strong>.</p><p>The importer checks the records before creating them. Invalid JSON, missing names, missing profile URLs, or invalid first-message dates will stop the batch until the data is corrected.</p><h3>Batch Import results</h3><p>When the batch finishes, the screen shows a summary of:</p><ul><li><strong>Created</strong> — new inquiries successfully added.</li><li><strong>Duplicate — skipped</strong> — an inquiry record already existed, so another one was not created.</li><li><strong>Failed</strong> — the record could not be created and the reason is shown.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Duplicates are skipped on purpose.</strong><br><br>Do not try to force a second Journey for the same inquiry. Use Search to find the existing record.</div><p>The <strong>Clear</strong> button clears the pasted batch and the displayed results.</p><h3>Admin Activity</h3><p><strong>Admin Activity</strong> is a shared activity view showing meaningful actions recorded by admins for the currently selected franchise locations.</p><p>Each activity row shows the time, admin, action, parent or Journey involved, and location.</p><p>Examples can include creating an inquiry, scheduling a visit or free trial, sending details to a franchise, recording a result, rescheduling, cancelling, scheduling a follow-up, recording enrollment, closing or reactivating a Journey, and sending another parent message.</p><p>The view follows the current <strong>Franchise Filter</strong>. If no franchise locations are selected, there is no activity to display.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Admin Activity is for visibility and accountability.</strong><br><br>Use the Parent Journey itself when you need the complete history and context for one parent.</div><h3>Location Performance</h3><p><strong>Location Performance</strong> is the reporting area intended to compare Journey outcomes by franchise location.</p><p>The view is structured around:</p><ul><li>Location</li><li>Inquiries</li><li>Trials</li><li>Enrolled</li><li>Trial → Enroll</li></ul><p>It follows the selected franchise locations when reporting rows are available.</p><p>In the current version, this area is a reporting view only and does not change Journey records. If no rows appear, there is no populated Location Performance report in the current build.</p><h3>Marketing Performance</h3><p><strong>Marketing Performance</strong> is the reporting area reserved for advertising performance and marketing snapshots.</p><p>The current screen includes a Marketing Performance view and an <strong>Enter New Snapshot</strong> control, but the completed snapshot-entry workflow is not yet active in this version of the app.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Do not rely on Marketing Performance as the system of record yet.</strong><br><br>Until the reporting workflow is completed, continue using the approved advertising records and processes already in place.</div><h3>Which Maintenance tool should I use?</h3><ul><li>Need to add many historical inquiries → <strong>Batch Import</strong>.</li><li>Need to see what admins have been doing → <strong>Admin Activity</strong>.</li><li>Need a location conversion reporting view → <strong>Location Performance</strong>.</li><li>Need advertising reporting or snapshots → <strong>Marketing Performance</strong> once that workflow is active.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Maintenance supports the Journey; it does not replace it.</strong><br><br>The main dashboard and Parent Journey remain the daily working system.</div>"},
{id:'common-situations',number:'14',title:'How to Handle Common Situations',summary:'Practical examples for situations admins encounter every day.',keywords:'slow reply direct enrollment changed mind missed trial cancellation duplicate returning parent',intro:'This section will cover common real-world situations such as slow replies, direct enrollment, missed trials, cancellations, duplicate inquiries, and old conversations returning.'},
{id:'rules-good-practices',number:'15',title:'Journey Rules and Good Practices',summary:'The operating rules that keep the Journey accurate and useful.',keywords:'rules best practices notes accuracy duplicate close slow reply',intro:'This section will define the habits that keep the system trustworthy, including keeping the stage aligned with reality and recording useful notes.'},
{id:'status-reference',number:'16',title:'Status and Action Reference',summary:'Plain-language meanings for statuses and next actions.',keywords:'status action reference new inquiry ready to send awaiting outcome follow-up due no longer interested',intro:'This section will provide a quick reference for the status and action labels used throughout Ads Journey.'},
{id:'troubleshooting',number:'17',title:'Troubleshooting / What If Something Is Wrong?',summary:'How to correct common mistakes without losing the journey history.',keywords:'troubleshooting wrong stage wrong appointment duplicate missing record accidental enrollment',intro:'This section will explain how to correct common problems such as a wrong stage, wrong appointment, accidental enrollment, duplicate journey, or missing record.'}
];
const tagalog={
about:{title:'Tungkol sa Ads Journey',summary:'Para saan ang Ads Journey at ano ang responsibilidad ng admin.',intro:'Ang Ads Journey ang pangunahing working system para sa pag-manage ng parent inquiries mula sa unang contact hanggang enrollment.',keywords:'layunin responsibilidad admin inquiry magulang record update',
content:"<h3>Ano ang Ads Journey</h3><p>Ang Ads Journey ang iisang working system para sa pag-manage ng bawat parent inquiry mula sa unang contact hanggang sa matapos ang journey sa enrollment o sa isang malinaw na closed outcome.</p><p>Maaaring sa Facebook Messenger pa rin nangyayari ang actual na usapan sa parent. Sa Ads Journey naman natin nire-record kung ano ang ibig sabihin ng usapang iyon sa trabaho: nasaan na ang parent sa journey, ano na ang nangyari, at ano ang kailangang mangyari next.</p><h3>Bakit natin ito ginagamit</h3><ul><li>Para hindi mawala ang inquiries at follow-ups.</li><li>Para pare-pareho ang nakikita ng lahat ng admin tungkol sa bawat parent.</li><li>Para may malinaw na history ng mahahalagang actions at outcomes.</li><li>Para malinaw ang next action at hindi nakaasa sa memorya, Messenger threads, o hiwa-hiwalay na sheets.</li><li>Para magkaroon tayo ng maaasahang impormasyon tungkol sa inquiries, trials, follow-ups, enrollments, at performance ng bawat location.</li></ul><h3>Responsibilidad mo bilang admin</h3><p>Ang trabaho mo ay hindi lang ilipat ang cards mula sa isang stage papunta sa iba. Ang trabaho mo ay panatilihing accurate ang bawat Journey.</p><ul><li>Siguraduhing ipinapakita ng Journey kung ano talaga ang nangyayari sa parent.</li><li>I-update ang Journey kapag may mahalagang pagbabago, gaya ng active conversation, scheduled visit o trial, result mula sa franchise, planned follow-up, enrollment, o malinaw na desisyon na hindi na ituloy.</li><li>Maglagay ng useful notes kapag makakatulong ito sa susunod na admin na maintindihan ang nangyari.</li><li>Gamitin ang Search bago gumawa ng bagong record kung posibleng existing na ang parent.</li><li>Huwag ilipat o i-close ang Journey para lang malinis ang isang column.</li></ul><h3>Ang pinakamahalagang rule</h3><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Dapat laging ipinapakita ng Journey kung ano talaga ang nangyayari sa parent ngayon.</strong><br><br>Kung active ang conversation, dapat iyon ang ipinapakita ng Journey. Kung may naka-book na trial, dapat Scheduled. Kung hinihintay natin ang result, dapat Awaiting Outcome. Kung nagdedesisyon pa ang parent, dapat Follow-up / Decision. Kapag nag-enroll, dapat Enrollment.</div><h3>Ano ang dapat makita sa isang magandang Journey record</h3><p>Kapag binuksan ng kahit sinong admin ang isang Journey, dapat sa loob lang ng ilang segundo ay malinaw na:</p><ul><li>Sino ang parent at anong location ang ini-inquire nila.</li><li>Anong stage na sila ngayon.</li><li>Ano ang huling mahalagang event.</li><li>Ano ang kailangang mangyari next.</li><li>Anong importanteng note ang makakaapekto sa pagpapatuloy ng conversation.</li></ul><h3>Isipin ang Journey bilang shared memory</h3><p>Hindi dapat nakaasa ang system sa isang admin na nakakaalala ng nangyari, naghahanap ng lumang Messenger thread, o tumitingin sa hiwalay na sheet. Kapag updated ang Journey, dapat kayang ipagpatuloy ng ibang admin ang trabaho nang hindi nanghuhula.</p>"},
'journey-at-a-glance':{title:'Buod ng Buong Journey',summary:'Paano gumagalaw ang inquiry mula unang contact hanggang enrollment.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag sa section na ito ang buong Journey sa simpleng paraan, kung paano dumadaan ang parent sa bawat stage, at bakit kailangan ang bawat stage.',keywords:'buod stages daloy inquiry enrollment active conversation scheduled outcome follow-up direct enrollment',
content:"<h3>Ang basic idea</h3><p>Ang bawat parent inquiry ay nagsisimula bilang isang Journey. Gumagalaw ang Journey habang nagbabago ang totoong sitwasyon ng parent.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Hindi checklist ang mga stages.</strong><br><br>Hindi kailangang dumaan ang parent sa lahat ng stages. Dapat ilipat ang Journey sa stage na pinakamalinaw na naglalarawan kung ano ang nangyayari ngayon.</div><h3>Stage 1 — Inquiry</h3><p>Dito nagsisimula ang bagong inquiry. Dito ginagawa ang unang contact, sinasagot ang unang questions, at inaalam kung ano talaga ang nangyayari sa lead.</p><p>Mula Stage 1, puwedeng mapunta ang Journey sa Continue Conversation, Scheduled, Enrollment, o No Longer Interested depende sa nangyari.</p><h3>Stage 1A — Continue Conversation</h3><p>Para ito sa totoong active conversation na patuloy pa rin pero wala pang scheduled visit, free trial, enrollment, o malinaw na ending.</p><p>Puwedeng mabilis o mabagal ang reply. Ang mahalaga ay genuinely engaged pa rin ang parent at buhay pa ang conversation.</p><h3>Stage 2 — Scheduled</h3><p>Nag-commit na ang parent sa isang visit o free trial. Naka-record ang appointment details at ipinapadala ang mga ito sa franchise.</p><p>Mananatili dito ang Journey habang hinihintay ang scheduled appointment.</p><h3>Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</h3><p>Dumating na ang oras ng scheduled visit o free trial at kailangan na nating malaman kung ano ang nangyari.</p><p>Kukunin ng admin ang result mula sa franchise at ire-record ang outcome.</p><h3>Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision</h3><p>Hindi pa enrolled ang parent pero may kailangan pang i-follow up o may decision pang hinihintay.</p><p>Kasama rito ang interested parent na kailangan pa ng oras, no-show, cancelled appointment, o ibang sitwasyon kung saan kailangan pang ipagpatuloy ang conversation.</p><h3>Stage 5 — Enrollment</h3><p>Nag-enroll na ang parent. Ito ang successful completion ng Journey.</p><h3>Hindi pare-pareho ang path ng bawat Journey</h3><p>Ilan sa mga common paths ay:</p><ul><li><strong>Inquiry → Continue Conversation → Scheduled → Awaiting Outcome → Follow-up / Decision → Enrollment</strong></li><li><strong>Inquiry → Scheduled → Awaiting Outcome → Enrollment</strong></li><li><strong>Inquiry → Continue Conversation → Enrollment</strong> kapag nag-enroll ang parent diretso kahit walang visit o free trial.</li><li><strong>Inquiry → No Longer Interested</strong> kapag malinaw na tumanggi ang parent o totoong natapos na ang Journey.</li><li><strong>Follow-up / Decision → Scheduled</strong> kapag may panibagong visit o free trial na naayos.</li></ul><h3>Ano ang nagpapagalaw sa Journey</h3><p>Gumagalaw ang Journey dahil may meaningful na nangyari sa totoong conversation o appointment — hindi dahil lumipas lang ang oras at hindi para lang malinis ang board.</p><ul><li>Nagsimula ang totoong conversation sa parent → Continue Conversation.</li><li>May na-book na visit o free trial → Scheduled.</li><li>Dumating na ang scheduled appointment time → Awaiting Outcome.</li><li>Kailangan pa ng parent follow-up pagkatapos ng result → Follow-up / Decision.</li><li>Nag-enroll ang parent → Enrollment.</li><li>Malinaw na tinapos ng parent ang conversation → No Longer Interested.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Kapag hindi ka sigurado kung anong stage ang gagamitin, itanong ito:</strong><br><br>“Ano talaga ang nangyayari sa parent na ito ngayon?”<br><br>Karaniwan, ang sagot ang magsasabi kung saang stage dapat ilagay ang Journey.</div>"},
'main-dashboard':{title:'Main Dashboard',summary:'Counters, working queue, Journey cards, at kung paano nakaayos ang board.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito ang nakikita sa main screen, ang ibig sabihin ng counters, kung paano gumagana ang stage columns, at kung paano nakaayos ang Journeys sa bawat stage.',keywords:'dashboard counters active scheduled franchise update due follow up enrolled board cards ayos due now',content:"<h3>Para saan ang dashboard</h3><p>Ang Main Dashboard ang pangunahing working view ng mga parent Journey na kasalukuyang kailangang i-manage. Dito mabilis mong makikita ang overall workload, kung nasaan ang bawat parent sa Journey, at alin ang kailangang unahin.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Working queue ang dashboard, hindi permanenteng listahan ng lahat ng records.</strong><br><br>Maaaring hindi na lumabas sa board ang older, closed, dormant, o completed records. Gamitin ang Search kapag kailangan mong hanapin ang Journey na hindi na visible sa board.</div><h3>Mga counter sa itaas</h3><p>Ang limang counters ay mabilis na summary ng mga location na kasalukuyang selected sa Franchise Filter.</p><ul><li><strong>Active</strong> — kabuuang Journeys na kasalukuyang visible sa working board.</li><li><strong>Scheduled</strong> — mga Journey sa Stage 2 na may scheduled visit o free trial.</li><li><strong>Franchise Update Due</strong> — mga Journey sa Stage 3 na dumating na ang scheduled time at kailangan na natin ang result mula sa franchise.</li><li><strong>Follow Up</strong> — mga Stage 4 Journey na due na ngayon ang parent follow-up. Hindi ito ang total number ng lahat ng records sa Stage 4.</li><li><strong>Enrolled</strong> — mga enrolled Journey na kasalukuyang ipinapakita pa sa working board.</li></ul><p>Kapag binago mo ang Franchise Filter, mag-a-update din ang board at counters ayon sa selected locations.</p><h3>Ang Working Queue</h3><p>Ang board ay nahahati sa anim na columns. Bawat column ay kumakatawan sa current stage ng parent:</p><ul><li><strong>Stage 1 — Inquiry</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 1A — Continue Conversation</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision</strong></li><li><strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong></li></ul><p>Ang number sa upper-right ng bawat column ay ang bilang ng Journeys na kasalukuyang visible sa stage na iyon.</p><h3>Pagbasa ng Journey card</h3><p>Bawat card ay isang parent Journey. Nagbibigay ang card ng sapat na information para malaman mo kung ano ang dapat tingnan next nang hindi kailangang buksan lahat ng records.</p><p>Depende sa stage, maaaring makita sa card ang:</p><ul><li>Facebook name ng parent.</li><li>Franchise location.</li><li>Current status.</li><li>Next action, gaya ng Continue Conversation, Send Details to Franchise, Get Result From Franchise, o Follow Up With Parent.</li><li>Date o time na konektado sa next action.</li></ul><p>Sa Stage 1, makikita kung kailan unang pumasok ang inquiry. Sa later stages, mas naka-focus ang card sa current status at sa susunod na kailangang gawin.</p><h3>Due now</h3><p>Kapag dumating na o lumampas na ang oras ng required action, maaaring magkaroon ang card ng <strong>Due now</strong> at mas maging visible ito sa board.</p><p>Hindi ibig sabihin nito na dapat automatic mong ilipat ang stage. Buksan ang Journey, alamin kung ano ang due, at gawin ang tamang real-world action.</p><h3>Paano nakaayos ang records</h3><p>Automatic na inaayos ng board ang bawat stage para unang makita ang pinakamahalagang records:</p><ul><li><strong>Inquiry</strong> — newest inquiries first.</li><li><strong>Continue Conversation</strong> — pinaka-recent na active conversations first.</li><li><strong>Scheduled</strong> — pinakamalapit na upcoming appointment o action first.</li><li><strong>Awaiting Outcome</strong> — pinakamalapit na due result first.</li><li><strong>Follow-up / Decision</strong> — pinakamalapit na due follow-up first.</li><li><strong>Enrollment</strong> — pinaka-recent na updated enrollments first.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Hindi mo kailangang manual na ayusin ang board.</strong><br><br>Panatilihing accurate ang bawat Journey at updated ang next action. Gagamitin ng dashboard ang information na iyon para mailagay at ma-order nang tama ang record.</div><h3>Pagbukas ng Journey</h3><p>I-click ang Journey card para buksan ito. Nasa Journey window ang detailed information, timeline, notes, current status, at mga actions na available para sa stage na iyon.</p><p>Ang dashboard ang nagbibigay ng overview. Ang Journey mismo ang ginagamit para maintindihan ang record at gawin ang susunod na update.</p><h3>Ibang controls sa dashboard</h3><p>Nasa itaas din ng dashboard ang New Inquiry, Search, Franchise Filter, Help, at Maintenance. May sariling sections ang mga tools na ito sa manual. Para sa normal na daily work, ang Working Queue ang dapat manatiling main view mo.</p>"},
'stage-1':{title:'Stage 1 — Inquiry',summary:'Mga bagong inquiry at ang unang decisions na kailangang gawin ng admin.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung ano ang dapat nasa Stage 1 at paano piliin ang tamang next step para sa bagong parent inquiry.',keywords:'bagong inquiry trial visit conversation enroll close parent child session schedule message',content:"<h3>Ano ang ibig sabihin ng Stage 1</h3><p>Sa Stage 1 nagsisimula ang bagong parent inquiry. Nakipag-contact na ang parent, nagawa na ang Journey, pero wala pang na-record na unang meaningful na decision.</p><p>Ang trabaho mo sa Stage 1 ay intindihin kung ano talaga ang nangyayari sa conversation at piliin ang next step na tugma sa totoong sitwasyon ng parent.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag ilipat ang Journey para lang mabawasan ang Stage 1.</strong><br><br>Piliin ang option na talagang naglalarawan sa nangyari sa parent.</div><h3>Pagbukas ng Stage 1 Journey</h3><p>I-click ang card ng parent sa Inquiry column. Magbubukas ang Journey window kung saan makikita ang parent, location, current stage, current status, next step, at Journey Timeline.</p><p>Sa ilalim ng <strong>Choose the next step</strong>, may apat na pangunahing choices: Free Trial, Visit, Continue Conversation, at Enroll. May hiwalay ding <strong>No Longer Interested</strong> action.</p><h3>Free Trial</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Free Trial</strong> kapag pumayag na ang parent sa isang specific na free trial appointment.</p><p>Ilagay ang appointment information:</p><ul><li><strong>Parent name</strong> — tunay na pangalan ng parent.</li><li><strong>Session interested in</strong> — piliin ang tamang session kapag alam na.</li><li><strong>Date at time</strong> — ang napagkasunduang trial schedule.</li><li><strong>Child name</strong> — required para sa appointment record.</li><li><strong>Age</strong> — years at months kapag alam.</li><li><strong>Notes</strong> — anumang useful information na dapat malaman ng franchise.</li></ul><p>Piliin ang <strong>Save Schedule</strong>. Lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>, kung saan gagawin ang franchise handoff.</p><h3>Visit</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Visit</strong> kapag pumayag ang parent na pumunta sa playschool para bumisita sa halip na mag-free trial.</p><p>Kumpletuhin ang parehong appointment information at piliin ang <strong>Save Schedule</strong>. Lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Mag-schedule lang ng visit o free trial kapag pumayag na talaga ang parent sa appointment.</strong><br><br>Huwag gumawa ng schedule dahil nag-suggest ka lang ng date o nagtanong kung gusto nilang bumisita.</div><h3>Continue Conversation</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Continue Conversation</strong> kapag genuinely engaged pa ang parent pero wala pang visit, free trial, enrollment, o malinaw na ending.</p><p>Puwede kang maglagay ng maikling Message Note tungkol sa ipinadalang message o sa pinag-uusapan. Optional ang note pero makakatulong ito para maintindihan ng ibang admin ang context.</p><p>Piliin ang <strong>Save to Stage 1A</strong>. Lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 1A — Continue Conversation</strong> at mare-record ang message sa Journey Timeline.</p><p>Halimbawa nito ang parent na nagtatanong pa tungkol sa rates, schedules, age groups, requirements, o available options bago magdesisyon kung ano ang next.</p><h3>Enroll</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Enroll</strong> kapag nag-enroll ang parent diretso mula sa inquiry o active conversation nang hindi na kailangan ng visit o free trial.</p><p>Puwede kang maglagay ng Enrollment Note, pagkatapos piliin ang <strong>Confirm Enrolled</strong>. Diretsong lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</p><p>Gamitin lang ang Enroll kapag totoong nangyari na ang enrollment. Ang pagiging interested, intensyon na mag-enroll, o pagsabi ng “gusto kong mag-enroll” ay hindi pa completed enrollment kung hindi pa natatapos ang required enrollment step.</p><h3>No Longer Interested</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>No Longer Interested</strong> kapag malinaw nang nagdesisyon ang parent na hindi ituloy at talagang tapos na ang Journey.</p><p>Required ang note. Ilagay ang reason o useful context, pagkatapos piliin ang <strong>Confirm No Longer Interested</strong>. Magsasara ang Journey at mawawala ito sa working board.</p><p>Huwag gamitin ang No Longer Interested dahil lang mabagal mag-reply ang parent. Ang mabagal na reply ay hindi pareho sa malinaw na desisyon na hindi na ituloy.</p><h3>Paano pumili ng tamang action</h3><ul><li>Pumayag ang parent sa free trial → <strong>Free Trial</strong>.</li><li>Pumayag ang parent sa visit → <strong>Visit</strong>.</li><li>Active pa ang conversation pero wala pang appointment o enrollment → <strong>Continue Conversation</strong>.</li><li>Totoong nag-enroll na ang parent → <strong>Enroll</strong>.</li><li>Malinaw nang tinapos ng parent ang inquiry → <strong>No Longer Interested</strong>.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang pinakamahalagang tanong ay: “Ano talaga ang nangyari sa parent na ito?”</strong><br><br>Ang sagot ang magsasabi kung anong Stage 1 action ang tama.</div><h3>Pagkatapos mag-save</h3><p>Automatic na mag-a-update ang dashboard. Lalabas ang Journey sa bagong stage nito, at magiging bahagi ng Journey Timeline ang action na ni-record mo para maintindihan ng ibang admin kung ano ang nangyari.</p>"},
'stage-1a':{title:'Stage 1A — Continue Conversation',summary:'Mga active na usapan sa parent na wala pang scheduled outcome.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung kailan dapat nasa Stage 1A ang Journey, paano panatilihing updated ang active conversation, at ano ang magpapalipat nito sa susunod na stage.',keywords:'active usapan reply message conversation free trial visit enroll no longer interested',content:"<h3>Ano ang ibig sabihin ng Stage 1A</h3><p>Ang Stage 1A ay para sa parent na genuinely engaged sa active conversation pero wala pang scheduled visit, free trial, enrollment, o malinaw na ending.</p><p>Maaaring nagtatanong pa ang parent, nagko-compare ng options, tumitingin ng schedules, nag-uusap tungkol sa rates, o nagdedesisyon kung ano ang bagay sa anak nila.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang Stage 1A ay nangangahulugang buhay pa ang conversation.</strong><br><br>Hindi kailangang agad mag-reply ang parent. Ang mahalaga ay may totoong conversation pa na kailangang ipagpatuloy.</div><h3>Paano napupunta ang Journey sa Stage 1A</h3><p>Karaniwang nanggagaling ito sa Stage 1 kapag pinili ng admin ang <strong>Continue Conversation</strong> at ni-record ang parent message o ongoing discussion.</p><p>Kapag nasa Stage 1A na, makikita ang card sa Continue Conversation column at ang next step ay mananatiling <strong>Continue Conversation</strong>.</p><h3>Pagbukas ng Stage 1A Journey</h3><p>I-click ang card ng parent sa Continue Conversation column. Makikita sa Journey window ang current stage, current status, next step, at Journey Timeline.</p><p>Available pa rin ang parehong action choices dahil maaaring humantong ang active conversation diretso sa Free Trial, Visit, Enrollment, o malinaw na closed outcome.</p><h3>Continue Conversation ulit</h3><p>Kung nagpadala ka ng panibagong meaningful message at active pa rin ang conversation, piliin ulit ang <strong>Continue Conversation</strong>.</p><p>Puwede kang maglagay ng Message Note tungkol sa ipinadala o sa nagbago. Kapag pinili ang <strong>Save to Stage 1A</strong>, mananatili ang Journey sa Stage 1A at madadagdag ang bagong message sa Journey Timeline.</p><p>Mahalaga ito dahil makikita na patuloy na inaasikaso ang conversation at may context ang susunod na admin tungkol sa pinakabagong meaningful contact.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Hindi kailangang gumawa ng bagong Journey sa bawat bagong message ng parent.</strong><br><br>Gamitin ang parehong Journey at idagdag ang meaningful updates sa timeline nito.</div><h3>Kapag nag-book ang parent ng Free Trial</h3><p>Kapag nagresulta ang active conversation sa confirmed free trial, piliin ang <strong>Free Trial</strong> at ilagay ang parent name, session, date, time, child name, age, at useful notes.</p><p>Piliin ang <strong>Save Schedule</strong>. Lilipat ang Journey mula Stage 1A papunta sa <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</p><h3>Kapag nag-book ang parent ng Visit</h3><p>Kung playschool visit naman ang kinonfirm ng parent, piliin ang <strong>Visit</strong>, kumpletuhin ang appointment details, at piliin ang <strong>Save Schedule</strong>.</p><p>Lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</p><h3>Kapag direktang nag-enroll ang parent</h3><p>Kung totoong natapos ang enrollment habang nasa active conversation at hindi na kailangan ng visit o free trial, piliin ang <strong>Enroll</strong>.</p><p>Maglagay ng Enrollment Note kung useful at piliin ang <strong>Confirm Enrolled</strong>. Diretsong lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</p><h3>Kapag hindi na interested ang parent</h3><p>Kung malinaw na sinabi ng parent na hindi na sila magpapatuloy, piliin ang <strong>No Longer Interested</strong>.</p><p>Required ang note para malinaw kung bakit natapos ang Journey. Pagkatapos ng confirmation, magsasara ang Journey at mawawala sa working board.</p><p>Huwag gamitin ito dahil lang tahimik ang parent nang sandali. Magkaiba ang quiet conversation at malinaw na desisyon na hindi na ituloy.</p><h3>Ano ang dapat manatili sa Stage 1A</h3><p>Panatilihin ang Journey sa Stage 1A habang active pa ang conversation at wala pang nangyayaring alinman sa mga ito:</p><ul><li>Wala pang confirmed visit o free trial.</li><li>Wala pang completed enrollment.</li><li>Hindi pa malinaw na tinapos ng parent ang inquiry.</li></ul><p>Halimbawa nito ang parent na nagtatanong pa, pinag-uusapan kung anong session ang bagay, kinakausap muna ang asawa, nagtatanong tungkol sa rates o requirements, o kailangan ng oras para magdesisyon pero engaged pa rin.</p><h3>Ano ang nagpapalabas sa Journey mula Stage 1A</h3><ul><li>Confirmed free trial → <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</li><li>Confirmed visit → <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong>.</li><li>Completed enrollment → <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</li><li>Malinaw na hindi na itutuloy → <strong>Journey closed as No Longer Interested</strong>.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag ilipat ang Journey dahil lang mabagal ang conversation.</strong><br><br>Ilipat lamang kapag nagbago ang totoong sitwasyon ng parent.</div>"},
'stage-2':{title:'Stage 2 — Scheduled',summary:'Visits, free trials, franchise handoff, reschedule, at cancellation.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung ano ang mangyayari pagkatapos ma-schedule ang visit o free trial, kasama ang franchise handoff, paghihintay sa appointment, reschedule, at cancellation.',keywords:'scheduled visit trial franchise handoff copy message mark sent waiting appointment reschedule cancel awaiting outcome',content:"<h3>Ano ang ibig sabihin ng Stage 2</h3><p>Ang Stage 2 ay nangangahulugang nag-commit na ang parent sa isang specific na <strong>visit o free trial</strong>. Naka-record na ang appointment at ang susunod na responsibility ay siguraduhing matatanggap ng franchise ang tamang details.</p><p>Mananatili ang Journey sa Scheduled habang hinihintay nating mangyari ang appointment.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang Scheduled ay dapat may totoong confirmed appointment.</strong><br><br>Huwag gamitin ang Stage 2 para sa suggested date, possible visit, o parent na hindi pa pumapayag.</div><h3>Kapag bagong pasok ang Journey sa Stage 2</h3><p>Pagkatapos ma-save ang visit o free trial mula Stage 1 o Stage 1A, lalabas ang <strong>Franchise Handoff</strong> section.</p><p>Makikita ang scheduled date at time, location, at appointment details na inilagay para sa parent at child.</p><p>Sa puntong ito ang status ay <strong>Ready to Send</strong> at ang next step ay <strong>Send Details to Franchise</strong>.</p><h3>I-check ang appointment details</h3><p>Bago mag-send, siguraduhing tama ang appointment information. Maaaring kasama sa prepared franchise message ang:</p><ul><li>Visit o Free Trial.</li><li>Parent name at Facebook name.</li><li>Child name at age.</li><li>Session.</li><li>Date at time.</li><li>Useful notes para sa franchise.</li></ul><p>Gamitin ang appointment details control kapag kailangan mong i-review ang complete information bago ito ipadala.</p><h3>Copy Message</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Copy Message</strong> para kopyahin ang prepared appointment information. I-send ang information sa tamang franchise gamit ang normal na franchise communication channel.</p><p>Ang pag-copy ng message ay <strong>hindi</strong> nangangahulugang na-notify na ang franchise. Kinopya lang nito ang prepared text.</p><h3>Mark as Sent</h3><p>Pagkatapos mo talagang maipadala ang appointment details sa franchise, piliin ang <strong>Mark as Sent</strong>.</p><p>Magiging <strong>Details Sent to Franchise</strong> ang Journey status at magiging <strong>Wait for Visit / Free Trial</strong> ang next step.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag pindutin ang Mark as Sent bago maipadala ang details.</strong><br><br>Ang button na ito ang system record na totoong na-notify na ang franchise.</div><h3>Expected franchise update</h3><p>Kapag marked as sent na ang details, ipapakita ng Journey ang expected franchise update time. Mananatili ang Journey sa Stage 2 habang hinihintay ang scheduled appointment.</p><p>Hindi mo kailangang manual na ilipat ang Journey kapag dumating ang appointment time. Kapag dumating ang expected time, automatic itong ililipat ng dashboard sa <strong>Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</strong> para makuha ang result mula sa franchise.</p><h3>Reschedule</h3><p>Gamitin ang <strong>Reschedule</strong> kapag matutuloy pa rin ang appointment pero nagbago ang session, date, o time.</p><p>Ilagay ang bagong:</p><ul><li>Session.</li><li>Date.</li><li>Time.</li><li>Note, kung useful, tungkol sa dahilan ng change.</li></ul><p>Piliin ang <strong>Save New Schedule</strong>. Mananatili ang Journey sa scheduled workflow gamit ang updated appointment information, at mare-record ang change sa Journey Timeline.</p><p>Kung natanggap na ng franchise ang lumang appointment details, siguraduhin ding maipadala sa kanila ang updated appointment information.</p><h3>Cancel Appointment</h3><p>Gamitin ang <strong>Cancel Appointment</strong> kapag hindi na matutuloy ang scheduled visit o free trial.</p><p>Required ang cancellation note. Ilagay kung bakit na-cancel ang appointment, pagkatapos piliin ang <strong>Confirm Cancel</strong>.</p><p>Mare-record ang cancelled appointment sa Journey history at hindi na ito ituturing na active scheduled appointment. Pagkatapos nito, maaaring magpatuloy ang Journey sa tamang follow-up o decision path depende sa totoong sitwasyon ng parent.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang cancellation ay hindi automatic na nangangahulugang hindi na interested ang parent.</strong><br><br>Maaaring mag-cancel dahil sa schedule, sakit, travel, o ibang temporary reason. I-record kung ano talaga ang nangyari at ituloy ang Journey ayon doon.</div><h3>Ano ang dapat i-check sa Stage 2</h3><ul><li>Tama ba ang appointment information?</li><li>Naipadala na ba talaga ang details sa franchise?</li><li>Ginamit ba ang Mark as Sent pagkatapos lang maipadala ang details?</li><li>Nagbago ba ang appointment at kailangan ng reschedule?</li><li>Na-cancel ba ang appointment?</li></ul><h3>Ano ang nagpapalabas sa Journey mula Stage 2</h3><p>Ang normal na path ay:</p><p><strong>Scheduled → Details Sent to Franchise → Wait for Visit / Free Trial → Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome</strong></p><p>Automatic na hina-handle ng system ang paglipat sa Stage 3 kapag dumating ang expected appointment/update time. Ang responsibility ng admin ay panatilihing accurate ang appointment at franchise handoff bago iyon mangyari.</p>"},
'stage-3':{title:'Stage 3 — Awaiting Outcome',summary:'Pagkuha ng result pagkatapos ng scheduled visit o free trial.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung kailan napupunta ang Journey sa Awaiting Outcome at paano i-record ang result na ibinibigay ng franchise pagkatapos ng appointment.',keywords:'result outcome franchise trial visit'},
'stage-4':{title:'Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision',summary:'Parent follow-up pagkatapos ng visit, trial, no-show, cancellation, o ibang decision point.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung bakit napupunta ang Journey sa Stage 4, paano i-manage ang follow-up, at ano ang magpapagalaw o magsasara sa Journey.',keywords:'follow up decision interested no show cancelled follow up later enrolled reschedule no longer interested due now',content:"<h3>Ano ang ibig sabihin ng Stage 4</h3><p>Ang Stage 4 ang ginagamit kapag hindi pa enrolled ang parent pero may totoong decision o follow-up pang kailangang i-manage.</p><p>Maaaring manggaling dito ang Journey pagkatapos ng franchise result gaya ng <strong>Interested</strong>, <strong>No Show</strong>, o <strong>Cancelled</strong>. Maaari rin itong manatili rito kapag nag-schedule ang admin ng panibagong parent follow-up.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang Stage 4 ay hindi waiting room para sa nakalimutang leads.</strong><br><br>Kung mananatili rito ang Journey, dapat may malinaw na dahilan at, kung kailangan, may totoong next follow-up date.</div><h3>Pagbukas ng Stage 4 Journey</h3><p>I-click ang card ng parent sa Follow-up / Decision column. Makikita sa Journey window ang previous appointment information, current status, next action, at Journey Timeline.</p><p>Depende sa nangyari dati, maaaring makita ang status na <strong>Follow-up Due</strong>, <strong>No Show</strong>, o <strong>Appointment Cancelled</strong>.</p><p>Ang Stage 4 actions ay:</p><ul><li><strong>Enrolled</strong></li><li><strong>Reschedule</strong></li><li><strong>Follow Up Later</strong></li><li><strong>No Longer Interested</strong></li></ul><h3>Follow Up Later</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Follow Up Later</strong> kapag tunay pa ring potential enrollment ang parent pero mas tamang gawin ang next conversation sa ibang date.</p><p>Ilagay ang follow-up date, time, at note tungkol sa dapat tandaan o sa sinabi ng parent.</p><p>Piliin ang <strong>Save Follow-up</strong>. Mananatili ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 4 — Follow-up / Decision</strong> at mare-record ang bagong follow-up time.</p><p>Kapag dumating ang follow-up time, magiging due ang card at maaaring makita bilang <strong>Due now</strong>. Kasama rin ito sa <strong>Follow Up</strong> counter sa dashboard.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag gamitin ang Follow Up Later nang walang totoong dahilan.</strong><br><br>Dapat ang date ay kung kailan talaga natin planong kontakin ulit ang parent, hindi para lang mailayo ang card.</div><h3>Reschedule</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Reschedule</strong> kapag may panibagong visit o free trial na napagkasunduan.</p><p>Ilagay ang session, bagong date, bagong time, at useful note kung kailangan. Piliin ang <strong>Reschedule</strong>.</p><p>Babalik ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 2 — Scheduled</strong> gamit ang bagong appointment details.</p><p>Dahil bagong confirmed appointment ito, magsisimula ulit ang franchise handoff at kailangang maipadala ang updated details sa franchise.</p><h3>Enrolled</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Enrolled</strong> kapag totoong natapos na ng parent ang enrollment habang nasa follow-up process.</p><p>Puwedeng maglagay ng Enrollment Note, pagkatapos piliin ang <strong>Confirm Enrolled</strong>. Lilipat ang Journey sa <strong>Stage 5 — Enrollment</strong>.</p><p>Kung na-undo dati ang enrollment at nag-enroll ulit ang parent, maaaring lumabas ang action bilang <strong>Re-Enroll</strong>. Gamitin lang ito kapag totoong confirmed ang bagong enrollment.</p><h3>No Longer Interested</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>No Longer Interested</strong> kapag malinaw nang nagdesisyon ang parent na hindi magpatuloy at wala nang meaningful reason para mag-follow up pa.</p><p>Required ang note. Ilagay kung bakit matatapos ang Journey, pagkatapos piliin ang <strong>Confirm No Longer Interested</strong>.</p><p>Magsasara ang Journey at mawawala sa active working board, pero mananatiling available ang history nito sa Search.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang walang reply ay hindi automatic na No Longer Interested.</strong><br><br>Gamitin ang actual conversation at context. Kung kailangan pa ng follow-up, i-schedule ito. I-close lang ang Journey kapag malinaw na iyon ang totoong sitwasyon.</div><h3>Mga common Stage 4 situations</h3><ul><li><strong>Interested after trial</strong> — nagustuhan ng parent pero kailangan pa ng oras → Follow Up Later.</li><li><strong>No Show</strong> — kontakin ang parent; kung gusto ng bagong appointment → Reschedule.</li><li><strong>Cancelled</strong> — alamin kung gusto nila ng bagong date; kung oo → Reschedule.</li><li><strong>Kailangan pa ng oras</strong> — mag-schedule ng reasonable next contact → Follow Up Later.</li><li><strong>Completed enrollment</strong> → Enrolled.</li><li><strong>Malinaw na tumanggi</strong> → No Longer Interested.</li></ul><h3>Paano malaman ang next action</h3><ul><li>Kailangan ng panibagong conversation sa ibang araw → <strong>Follow Up Later → mananatili sa Stage 4</strong>.</li><li>Confirmed ang bagong visit o free trial → <strong>Reschedule → Stage 2</strong>.</li><li>Natapos ang enrollment → <strong>Enrolled → Stage 5</strong>.</li><li>Malinaw nang tapos ang Journey → <strong>No Longer Interested → closed</strong>.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang purpose ng Stage 4 ay panatilihing gumagalaw ang tunay na opportunity nang hindi ito nawawala.</strong><br><br>Bawat Journey dito ay dapat may malinaw na next action o malinaw na ending.</div>"},
'stage-5':{title:'Stage 5 — Enrollment',summary:'Ang successful ending ng Journey at paano i-correct ang enrollment kung kinakailangan.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung ano ang ibig sabihin ng Stage 5, anong information ang makikita pagkatapos ng enrollment, at paano mag-correct nang hindi nawawala ang Journey history.',keywords:'enrollment enrolled enrollment reported undo re-enroll correction timeline',content:"<h3>Ano ang ibig sabihin ng Stage 5</h3><p>Ang Stage 5 ay nangangahulugang totoong nag-enroll na ang parent. Ito ang successful completion ng advertising Journey.</p><p>Maaaring makarating ang Journey sa Stage 5 diretso mula Stage 1 o Stage 1A, mula sa franchise result sa Stage 3, o mula Stage 4 habang nagfo-follow up.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>I-record lang ang Enrollment kapag totoong nangyari na ang enrollment.</strong><br><br>Ang pagiging interested, pangakong mag-e-enroll, o pagtatanong kung paano mag-enroll ay hindi pa enrollment. Dapat totoong completed enrollment ang Stage 5.</div><h3>Pagbukas ng enrolled Journey</h3><p>I-click ang card sa Enrollment column para buksan ang Journey.</p><p>Makikita sa Enrollment section ang:</p><ul><li>Parent at franchise location.</li><li>Child name kung na-record ito earlier sa Journey.</li><li>Date at time kung kailan ni-report ang enrollment.</li><li>Enrollment note na ni-record.</li><li>Complete Journey Timeline na nagpapakita kung paano umabot ang parent sa enrollment.</li></ul><p>Makikita ang Journey stage bilang <strong>Enrolled</strong>. Depende sa current processing state, maaari ring ipakita ng status na na-report na ang enrollment.</p><h3>Bakit mahalaga pa rin ang Journey history</h3><p>Enrollment ang final result, pero mahalaga pa rin ang history bago ito. Maaaring makita sa timeline ang original inquiry, conversations, appointments, franchise handoffs, trial o visit results, follow-ups, at sa huli ang enrollment.</p><p>Nagbibigay ito ng reliable record kung ano talaga ang nagdala sa successful outcome at nagiging useful ang Journey later para sa performance at analysis.</p><h3>Undo Enrollment</h3><p>Gamitin lang ang <strong>Undo Enrollment</strong> kapag mali ang pagkaka-record ng enrollment o kailangan talagang i-correct ang current situation.</p><p>Piliin ang <strong>Undo Enrollment</strong>, ilagay ang reason ng correction, pagkatapos piliin ang <strong>Confirm Undo</strong>.</p><p>Required ang reason. Ire-record ng system ang enrollment reversal sa Journey Timeline sa halip na burahin ang original enrollment history.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Correction tool ang Undo Enrollment, hindi normal na Journey action.</strong><br><br>Huwag mag-undo ng enrollment dahil lang may nagbago pagkatapos. Gamitin ito kapag ang enrollment record mismo ay hindi na dapat ituring na current outcome.</div><h3>Ano ang mangyayari pagkatapos ng Undo Enrollment</h3><p>Babalik ang Journey sa active follow-up flow para ma-handle nang tama ang current situation ng parent.</p><p>Mananatiling visible sa Journey history ang previous enrollment kasama ang reason kung bakit ito na-undo. Kung mag-enroll ulit ang parent later, maaaring makita sa Stage 4 ang action na <strong>Re-Enroll</strong>.</p><h3>Re-Enroll</h3><p>Ginagamit ang <strong>Re-Enroll</strong> kapag na-undo ang dating enrollment at pagkatapos ay totoong nag-enroll ulit ang parent.</p><p>I-confirm ang bagong enrollment tulad ng normal na enrollment. Madadagdag ang bagong enrollment sa Journey history para mapanatili ang buong sequence sa halip na palitan ang dating events.</p><h3>Ano ang dapat i-check bago mag-record ng Enrollment</h3><ul><li>Totoo bang natapos ng parent ang required enrollment step?</li><li>Tamang parent at franchise location ba ito?</li><li>May useful enrollment note bang dapat i-record?</li><li>Real enrollment ba ang nire-record at hindi lamang interest o intent?</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Dapat mapagkakatiwalaan ang Stage 5.</strong><br><br>Bawat Journey na nire-record bilang enrolled ay nagiging bahagi ng enrollment at conversion information natin. Direktang naaapektuhan ng accuracy dito kung paano natin naiintindihan ang franchise at advertising performance.</div>"},
'reading-a-journey':{title:'Pagbukas at Pagbasa ng Journey',summary:'Paano mabilis maintindihan ang isang Journey bago gumawa ng action.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung paano basahin ang Journey window para mabilis maintindihan kung sino ang parent, ano ang nangyayari ngayon, ano ang nangyari dati, at ano ang dapat gawin next.',keywords:'basa journey parent location child stage status next step action timeline history notes appointment details',content:"<h3>Pagbukas ng Journey</h3><p>I-click ang anumang Journey card sa dashboard para buksan ang buong Parent Journey.</p><p>Pinagsasama ng Journey panel ang current situation at important history sa iisang lugar. Bago gumawa ng action, basahin muna ang Journey.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag magsimula sa pagpindot ng action button.</strong><br><br>Intindihin muna ang parent, current stage, current status, next step, at recent timeline.</div><h3>1. Parent information</h3><p>Sa itaas ng Journey makikita ang parent at location information.</p><ul><li><strong>Parent name</strong> — karaniwang Facebook name o real parent name kapag na-capture na.</li><li><strong>Franchise location</strong> — ang location na kinabibilangan ng inquiry.</li><li><strong>Facebook name</strong> — ipinapakita kasama ng location para maitugma ang Journey sa Messenger conversation.</li><li><strong>Child name</strong> — makikita kapag na-record ito habang nagsa-schedule o sa ibang bahagi ng Journey.</li></ul><p>Nakakatulong ito para masigurong tamang parent ang inaasikaso mo bago gumawa ng pagbabago.</p><h3>2. Journey Stage</h3><p>Ang <strong>Journey Stage</strong> ang nagsasabi kung nasaan ang parent ngayon sa overall process.</p><p>Halimbawa: New Inquiry, Continue Conversation, Appointment Scheduled, Awaiting Franchise Update, Parent Follow-up, at Enrolled.</p><p>Sinasagot ng stage ang tanong na: <strong>“Nasaan ngayon ang parent sa Journey?”</strong></p><h3>3. Current Status</h3><p>Ang <strong>Current Status</strong> ay nagbibigay ng mas specific na information tungkol sa nangyayari sa loob ng stage.</p><p>Halimbawa: New Inquiry, Active Conversation, Ready to Send to Franchise, Details Sent to Franchise, Waiting for Franchise Result, Follow-up Due, No Show, Appointment Cancelled, at Enrolled.</p><p>Sinasagot ng status ang: <strong>“Ano ang current condition ng Journey na ito?”</strong></p><h3>4. Next Step</h3><p>Ang <strong>Next Step</strong> ang nagsasabi kung ano ang inaasahang mangyari next.</p><p>Halimbawa: Continue Conversation, Send Details to Franchise, Wait for Visit / Free Trial, Get Result From Franchise, Follow Up With Parent, o No Action Needed.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Magkakasamang binabasa ang Stage, Status, at Next Step.</strong><br><br>Ang Stage ang nagsasabi kung nasaan ang parent. Ang Status ang nagsasabi kung ano ang nangyayari roon. Ang Next Step ang nagsasabi kung ano ang dapat mangyari next.</div><h3>5. Action area</h3><p>Nagbabago ang gitnang bahagi ng Journey depende sa current stage. Ang ipinapakita lang dito ay ang actions na may sense para sa stage na iyon.</p><p>Halimbawa:</p><ul><li>Sa Stage 1 at Stage 1A makikita ang Free Trial, Visit, Continue Conversation, Enroll, at No Longer Interested.</li><li>Sa Stage 2 makikita ang franchise handoff, appointment details, Mark as Sent, Reschedule, at Cancel Appointment.</li><li>Sa Stage 3 makikita ang franchise result choices at Reschedule.</li><li>Sa Stage 4 makikita ang Enrolled, Reschedule, Follow Up Later, at No Longer Interested.</li><li>Sa Stage 5 makikita ang enrollment record at Undo Enrollment.</li></ul><p>Piliin ang action na tugma sa totoong nangyari. Huwag pumili dahil available lang ang button.</p><h3>6. Appointment at detail sections</h3><p>Kung may visit o free trial ang Journey, maaaring ipakita ng panel ang scheduled date at time, location, appointment type, parent at child information, session, at notes.</p><p>Gamitin ang expandable appointment details kapag kailangan mong i-review ang original information o maintindihan ang later reschedule, cancellation, no-show, o follow-up.</p><h3>7. Journey Timeline</h3><p>Ang <strong>Journey Timeline</strong> ang history ng meaningful events sa Journey. Nauuna ang newest events.</p><p>Maaaring kasama sa timeline ang:</p><ul><li>Inquiry created.</li><li>Message sent to parent.</li><li>Visit o free trial scheduled.</li><li>Details sent to franchise.</li><li>Appointment rescheduled o cancelled.</li><li>No show.</li><li>Visit o trial completed.</li><li>Parent interested o not interested.</li><li>Follow-up scheduled o completed.</li><li>Enrollment reported, undone, o processed.</li><li>Journey closed, dormant, o reactivated.</li></ul><p>Maaaring may kasama ring note, appointment information, o date at time ang bawat timeline entry.</p><h3>Paano mabilis basahin ang Journey</h3><p>Kapag nagbukas ka ng record, sundin ang order na ito:</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> I-confirm ang parent at franchise.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> Basahin ang Journey Stage.</li><li><strong>3.</strong> Basahin ang Current Status.</li><li><strong>4.</strong> Basahin ang Next Step.</li><li><strong>5.</strong> Tingnan ang pinakabagong Timeline entries.</li><li><strong>6.</strong> I-review ang appointment details o notes kung kailangan.</li><li><strong>7.</strong> Gawin ang tamang action.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Dapat maintindihan ang isang good Journey kahit hindi mo na tanungin ang ibang admin kung ano ang nangyari.</strong><br><br>Kapag accurate ang stage, status, next step, at timeline, dapat kayang buksan ng kahit sinong admin ang Journey at ipagpatuloy ang trabaho nang hindi nanghuhula.</div>"},
search:{title:'Search',summary:'Paghahanap ng active, closed, enrolled, dormant, at lumang Journeys.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung paano hanapin ang Journeys na wala sa current working board, i-review ang history, at i-reactivate ang closed Journey kapag bumalik ang parent.',keywords:'hanap facebook profile url username name inquiry id journey id parent child active closed dormant enrolled view record open reactivate duplicate lumang record',content:"<h3>Para saan ang Search</h3><p>Working queue ang dashboard kaya hindi lahat ng Journey ay palaging makikita roon. Sa <strong>Search</strong>, puwedeng hanapin ang records lampas sa current board, kasama ang active, dormant, enrolled, closed, at older Journeys.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Gamitin ang Search bago gumawa ng bagong Journey kung sa tingin mo ay maaaring may existing record na ang parent.</strong><br><br>Nakakatulong ito para maiwasan ang duplicate records at manatili sa iisang Journey ang buong history ng parent.</div><h3>Pagbukas ng Search</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>Search</strong> sa itaas ng dashboard. Magbubukas ang Journey Search window na may search box.</p><p>Maaaring mag-search gamit ang:</p><ul><li>Facebook profile URL.</li><li>Facebook username.</li><li>Parent o Facebook name.</li><li>Child name.</li><li>Inquiry ID.</li><li>Journey ID.</li></ul><p>Ilagay ang information na alam mo at piliin ang <strong>Search</strong>, o pindutin ang Enter.</p><h3>Pagbasa ng search results</h3><p>Makikita sa bawat result ang parent, franchise location, Journey stage, current status, at record state.</p><p>Ang record state ang nagsasabi kung ang Journey ay:</p><ul><li><strong>Active</strong> — active work pa ang Journey.</li><li><strong>Closed</strong> — dati nang natapos ang Journey.</li><li><strong>Dormant</strong> — naka-save ang record sa history pero hindi ito kasalukuyang active board work.</li></ul><p>Makikita rin sa Search ang enrolled at older records kahit wala na sila sa working board.</p><h3>View Record</h3><p>Piliin ang <strong>View Record</strong> kapag gusto mong i-review ang Journey nang walang binabago.</p><p>Mag-e-expand ang result at ipapakita ang current stage, current status, Facebook name, at Journey history. Makikita sa history ang meaningful events at notes mula newest hanggang older events.</p><p>Piliin ang <strong>Hide Record</strong> para isara ulit ang details.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>View Record ang pinakaligtas na unang step kapag hindi ka sigurado kung tamang parent ang nakita mo.</strong><br><br>I-review muna ang history bago mag-open, reactivate, o gumawa ng bagong record.</div><h3>Pag-open ng active Journey</h3><p>Kung Active ang result, may <strong>Open</strong> button.</p><p>Kung visible ang Journey sa currently selected franchise board, isasara ng Open ang Search at bubuksan ang normal Parent Journey panel para maipagpatuloy mo ang trabaho.</p><p>Kung active ang Journey pero hindi kasalukuyang visible sa selected franchise board, sasabihin iyon ng Search sa halip na buksan ang maling board record.</p><h3>Pag-reactivate ng closed Journey</h3><p>Kung bumalik ang parent na may closed Journey at dapat ipagpatuloy ang dati niyang Journey, piliin ang <strong>Reactivate Journey</strong>.</p><p>Ire-record ng system ang reactivation, ire-reload ang working board, at ia-update ang search result. Mananatili ang lumang history para konektado ang bagong conversation sa mga nangyari dati.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>I-reactivate ang existing Journey kapag continuation ito ng dating conversation ng parehong parent.</strong><br><br>Huwag gumawa ng bagong Journey dahil lang closed ang luma.</div><h3>Dormant Journeys</h3><p>Mahahanap at mare-review ang Dormant Journeys sa Search. Makikita ang label na <strong>Dormant journey</strong> at hindi ito binubuksan bilang normal active board work mula sa Search result.</p><p>Gamitin ang View Record para maintindihan ang history bago magdesisyon kung ano ang dapat mangyari next.</p><h3>Search at Franchise Filter</h3><p>Mas malawak ang Search kaysa sa visible working board. Ang pagkakita ng record sa Search ay hindi nangangahulugang currently selected ang franchise nito sa dashboard.</p><p>Kaya posibleng may Active Search result kahit hindi nakikita ang card nito sa current board view.</p><h3>Kapag may duplicate na nakita sa New Inquiry</h3><p>Kung ma-detect ng New Inquiry na may inquiry record na ang Facebook profile, maaaring lumabas ang <strong>Open Existing Journey</strong>.</p><p>Kapag posible, hahanapin ng app ang existing Journey, isasama ang franchise nito sa current selection, ire-reload ang board, at bubuksan ang existing record. Kung hindi ito mabuksan diretso, dadalhin ka sa Search kung saan makikita ang record.</p><h3>Simple Search routine</h3><ul><li>Hanapin muna ang parent bago gumawa ng duplicate.</li><li>Gamitin ang View Record para i-confirm ang identity at history.</li><li>Kung Active, gamitin ang Open kapag nasa current board ang Journey.</li><li>Kung Closed at continuation ito ng parehong Journey, gamitin ang Reactivate Journey.</li><li>Kung Dormant, i-review muna ang record bago magdesisyon kung ano ang next.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Continuity ang goal ng Search.</strong><br><br>Hangga’t maaari, gusto natin ng isang accurate history para sa parent, hindi magkakahiwalay na records na nagpapahirap maintindihan ang totoong Journey.</div>"},
'franchise-filter':{title:'Franchise Filter',summary:'Pagpili kung aling locations ang kasalukuyang nakikita mo.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung paano binabago ng Franchise Filter ang records na ipinapakita sa dashboard at paano magtrabaho sa isa o maraming locations.',keywords:'filter location branch pili'},
maintenance:{title:'Maintenance',summary:'Batch Import, Admin Activity, Location Performance, at Marketing Performance.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito ang tools sa ilalim ng Maintenance, para saan ang bawat isa, at kailan sila dapat gamitin.',keywords:'maintenance batch import json backfill duplicate admin activity location performance marketing performance reporting snapshot',content:"<h3>Para saan ang Maintenance</h3><p>Ang <strong>Maintenance</strong> menu ay may tools na sumusuporta sa Ads Journey system pero hindi bahagi ng normal na parent-by-parent workflow.</p><p>Ginagamit ito para sa pag-backfill ng inquiry records, pag-review ng admin activity, at pagtingin sa reporting areas.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag gamitin ang Maintenance tools bilang kapalit ng normal Journey workflow.</strong><br><br>Ang new inquiries, conversations, scheduling, outcomes, follow-ups, at enrollments ay dapat pa ring i-handle sa main Journey system.</div><h3>Batch Import</h3><p>Ang <strong>Batch Import</strong> ay backfill tool para gumawa ng maraming inquiry records para sa isang franchise nang sabay-sabay.</p><p>Gamitin ito kapag may historical o externally prepared inquiries na kailangang idagdag sa Ads Journey nang bulk sa halip na isa-isang ilagay sa New Inquiry.</p><h3>Paano gamitin ang Batch Import</h3><p>Buksan ang <strong>Maintenance → Batch Import</strong>, pagkatapos:</p><ul><li>Piliin ang <strong>Branch / location</strong> para sa buong batch.</li><li>I-paste ang inquiry records bilang <strong>JSON array</strong>.</li><li>Piliin ang <strong>Import Batch</strong>.</li></ul><p>Kailangang mayroon ang bawat record ng:</p><ul><li><strong>facebook_name</strong></li><li><strong>facebook_profile_url</strong></li><li><strong>first_message_at</strong></li></ul><p>Optional ang <strong>facebook_username</strong>, <strong>ad_id</strong>, <strong>inquiry_type</strong>, at <strong>initial_note</strong>.</p><p>Chine-check muna ng importer ang records bago gumawa. Kapag invalid ang JSON, kulang ang name o profile URL, o mali ang first-message date, hihinto ang batch hanggang ma-correct ang data.</p><h3>Batch Import results</h3><p>Pagkatapos ng batch, makikita ang summary ng:</p><ul><li><strong>Created</strong> — successful na na-create na bagong inquiries.</li><li><strong>Duplicate — skipped</strong> — may existing inquiry record na kaya hindi gumawa ng pangalawa.</li><li><strong>Failed</strong> — hindi na-create ang record at makikita ang dahilan.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Intentional ang pag-skip ng duplicates.</strong><br><br>Huwag piliting gumawa ng pangalawang Journey para sa parehong inquiry. Gamitin ang Search para hanapin ang existing record.</div><p>Nililinis ng <strong>Clear</strong> button ang pasted batch at displayed results.</p><h3>Admin Activity</h3><p>Ang <strong>Admin Activity</strong> ay shared activity view ng meaningful actions na ni-record ng admins para sa currently selected franchise locations.</p><p>Makikita sa bawat activity row ang time, admin, action, parent o Journey, at location.</p><p>Kasama sa mga halimbawa ang paggawa ng inquiry, pag-schedule ng visit o free trial, pagpapadala ng details sa franchise, pag-record ng result, reschedule, cancellation, follow-up scheduling, enrollment, pag-close o reactivate ng Journey, at pagpapadala ng panibagong parent message.</p><p>Sinusunod ng view ang current <strong>Franchise Filter</strong>. Kung walang selected franchise locations, walang activity na maipapakita.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Ang Admin Activity ay para sa visibility at accountability.</strong><br><br>Gamitin ang Parent Journey mismo kapag kailangan mo ang complete history at context ng isang parent.</div><h3>Location Performance</h3><p>Ang <strong>Location Performance</strong> ay reporting area para maikumpara ang Journey outcomes ayon sa franchise location.</p><p>Naka-structure ang view sa:</p><ul><li>Location</li><li>Inquiries</li><li>Trials</li><li>Enrolled</li><li>Trial → Enroll</li></ul><p>Sinusunod nito ang selected franchise locations kapag may available reporting rows.</p><p>Sa current version, reporting view lamang ito at hindi ito nagbabago ng Journey records. Kung walang rows na lumalabas, wala pang populated Location Performance report sa current build.</p><h3>Marketing Performance</h3><p>Ang <strong>Marketing Performance</strong> ay reporting area na nakalaan para sa advertising performance at marketing snapshots.</p><p>May Marketing Performance view at <strong>Enter New Snapshot</strong> control ang current screen, pero hindi pa active ang completed snapshot-entry workflow sa version na ito ng app.</p><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Huwag muna gamitin ang Marketing Performance bilang system of record.</strong><br><br>Hangga’t hindi pa complete ang reporting workflow, gamitin pa rin ang approved advertising records at processes na kasalukuyang ginagamit.</div><h3>Aling Maintenance tool ang gagamitin?</h3><ul><li>Kailangang magdagdag ng maraming historical inquiries → <strong>Batch Import</strong>.</li><li>Kailangang makita kung ano ang ginawa ng admins → <strong>Admin Activity</strong>.</li><li>Kailangang makita ang location conversion reporting → <strong>Location Performance</strong>.</li><li>Kailangang advertising reporting o snapshots → <strong>Marketing Performance</strong> kapag active na ang workflow.</li></ul><div class='help-manual-note'><strong>Sumusuporta ang Maintenance sa Journey; hindi nito pinapalitan ang Journey.</strong><br><br>Ang main dashboard at Parent Journey pa rin ang daily working system.</div>"},
'common-situations':{title:'Paano Harapin ang Karaniwang Sitwasyon',summary:'Practical examples para sa mga sitwasyong madalas makita ng admins.',intro:'Sasaklawin dito ang mga common situations gaya ng mabagal na reply, direct enrollment, missed trial, cancellation, duplicate inquiry, at pagbabalik ng lumang conversation.',keywords:'mabagal reply direct enrollment missed trial cancel duplicate bumalik'},
'rules-good-practices':{title:'Journey Rules at Good Practices',summary:'Mga operating rules para manatiling accurate at useful ang Journey.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito ang habits na nagpapanatiling maaasahan ang system, kasama ang pagpapanatiling tugma ng stage sa totoong nangyayari at pag-record ng useful notes.',keywords:'rules practice accurate notes duplicate close'},
'status-reference':{title:'Status at Action Reference',summary:'Simpleng paliwanag sa statuses at next actions.',intro:'Magbibigay ang section na ito ng mabilis na reference para sa status at action labels na ginagamit sa buong Ads Journey.',keywords:'status action reference labels'},
troubleshooting:{title:'Troubleshooting / Kapag May Mali',summary:'Paano ayusin ang common mistakes nang hindi nawawala ang Journey history.',intro:'Ipapaliwanag dito kung paano ayusin ang mga problemang gaya ng maling stage, maling appointment, accidental enrollment, duplicate Journey, o missing record.',keywords:'mali stage appointment enrollment duplicate missing record'}
};
let currentId='about';
function q(id){return document.getElementById(id);}
const LANGUAGE_KEY='ads_journey_help_language';
let language=localStorage.getItem(LANGUAGE_KEY)==='tl'?'tl':'en';
function localized(section,key){return language==='tl'?(tagalog[section.id]?.[key]||section[key]):section[key];}
function updateLanguageControls(){
  const english=q('helpLangEnglish'),tagalogButton=q('helpLangTagalog'),search=q('helpManualSearch');
  if(english)english.classList.toggle('active',language==='en');
  if(tagalogButton)tagalogButton.classList.toggle('active',language==='tl');
  if(search)search.placeholder=language==='tl'?'Hanapin sa manual':'Search the manual';
}
function setLanguage(next){
  language=next==='tl'?'tl':'en';localStorage.setItem(LANGUAGE_KEY,language);updateLanguageControls();renderToc(q('helpManualSearch')?.value||'');selectSection(currentId);
}
function renderToc(filter=''){
  const toc=q('helpManualToc');if(!toc)return;
  const term=filter.trim().toLowerCase();
  const visible=sections.filter(s=>{const t=tagalog[s.id]||{};const haystack=`${s.title} ${s.summary} ${s.keywords} ${s.intro} ${t.title||''} ${t.summary||''} ${t.keywords||''} ${t.intro||''}`.toLowerCase();return !term||haystack.includes(term);});
  if(!visible.length){toc.innerHTML=`<div class="help-manual-empty">${language==='tl'?'Walang section na tumutugma sa search.':'No manual sections match that search.'}</div>`;return;}
  toc.innerHTML='';
  visible.forEach(section=>{const button=document.createElement('button');button.type='button';button.className='help-manual-link'+(section.id===currentId?' active':'');button.dataset.manualId=section.id;button.innerHTML=`<span>${language==='tl'?'Seksyon':'Section'} ${section.number}</span>${localized(section,'title')}`;button.addEventListener('click',()=>selectSection(section.id));toc.appendChild(button);});
}
function renderPage(section){
  const page=q('helpManualPage');if(!page)return;
  const translated=tagalog[section.id]||{};
  const body=language==='tl'?(translated.content||`<h3>Ano ang sakop ng section na ito</h3><p>${localized(section,'intro')}</p><div class="help-manual-note">Binubuo natin ang manual section by section. Handa na ang page na ito para sa final instructions.</div>`):(section.content||`<h3>What this section will cover</h3><p>${section.intro}</p><div class="help-manual-note">We are building the manual section by section. This page is ready for its finalized instructions.</div>`);
  page.innerHTML=`<div class="help-manual-page"><p class="section-kicker">${language==='tl'?'Seksyon':'Section'} ${section.number}</p><h2>${localized(section,'title')}</h2><p class="manual-summary">${localized(section,'summary')}</p>${body}</div>`;
}
function selectSection(id){
  const section=sections.find(s=>s.id===id)||sections[0];currentId=section.id;renderPage(section);renderToc(q('helpManualSearch')?.value||'');q('helpManualPage')?.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'});
}
function init(){
  const search=q('helpManualSearch');if(!search)return;
  updateLanguageControls();
  if(search.dataset.ready==='1'){renderToc(search.value);renderPage(sections.find(s=>s.id===currentId)||sections[0]);return;}
  search.dataset.ready='1';
  search.addEventListener('input',()=>renderToc(search.value));
  q('helpLangEnglish')?.addEventListener('click',()=>setLanguage('en'));
  q('helpLangTagalog')?.addEventListener('click',()=>setLanguage('tl'));
  renderToc();renderPage(sections[0]);
}
window.openHelpManualTopic=function(id){const button=q('helpButton');if(button)button.click();setTimeout(()=>{init();selectSection(id);},0);};
window.getHelpManualTopic=function(id){return sections.find(s=>s.id===id)||null;};
window.addEventListener('click',event=>{if(event.target.closest('#helpButton'))setTimeout(init,0);});
init();
})();